  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100937004-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention of the above-described configuration is disposed on the reservoir water and subjected to the electrolysis and electrocoagulation treatment, the precipitation treatment, and the microbial treatment and the vegetation filtration decomposition of the green algae propagated water, thereby completely eliminating the green algae remaining in the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100937004-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, because no chemicals are used to remove the algae in the water, secondary pollution is not generated by the treated water returned to the reservoir, and the water treatment is purely electrolysis and electrocoagulation, precipitation, biochemical treatment by microorganisms, and aquatic life"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715020-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an electrolysis device installed in the aerobic iron precipitation tank, the electrolysis module having an electrode mounted thereon, and an insoluble precipitate precipitated by reaction of an oxide produced by electrolysis of the electrolysis module and phosphate contained in the mixed solution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715020-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the organic material and phosphorus are removed by the oxygen-free tank 40, the aerobic iron precipitation tank 50, and the electrolysis device 60, and nitrogen is removed in the nitrification and denitrification"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100715020-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the aerobic iron precipitation tank 50 removes organic substances by metabolic activity of microorganisms, oxidizes ammonia nitrogen and nitrite nitrogen to nitrate nitrogen by oxygen supplied through a blower, and causes electrolysis of iron or aluminum electrodes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102636761-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and, for example, when the integrated value of the current i after switching the polarity of each feeder 41, 42 and the flow path switching valve 85 is less than a predetermined threshold, precipitation of scale occurs with respect to the number of times of electrolysis"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102636761-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and the flow path switching valve (85) is greater than the predetermined threshold, the amount of scale precipitation is relatively large relative to the number of times of electrolysis"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102636761-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and the flow path switching valve (85) is less than a predetermined threshold value, the scale of the number of electrolysis the amount of precipitation can be estimated to be relatively large"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102636761-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and the flow path switching valve (85) is greater than the predetermined threshold, the amount of scale precipitation relative to the number of times of electrolysis is it can be estimated to be relatively small"}]</data>
