  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-9120685-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the provision of large evaporator sump volume such as that provided in the technology currently used for these applications would provide residence time for silicate precipitation and would increase rates of silica scaling"}, {"pat_id": "US-9120685-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(see table 1) the primary shortcoming of the conventional technology is that the evaporator will still experience scaling of the tube surface, because the precipitation is not completed in the evaporator sump and a portion of the precipitation reactions occur at the tube surface"}, {"pat_id": "US-9120685-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, it turns out that with this process scaling of the evaporator cannot be eliminated because it is impractical to make sump sizes large enough to achieve the necessary residence time for precipitation in the sump"}, {"pat_id": "US-9120685-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is noted that the provision of large evaporator sump volume such as that provided in the technology currently applied, would provide residence time for silicate precipitation and would increase rates of silica scaling"}]</data>
</edge>
