  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-7527736-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the system also includes a flotation separator that separates contaminants from the aerator effluent to produce a reclaimed water stream suitable for use as fracturing water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100546061-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, in sewage or polluted small streams, contaminants are deposited on the bottom in sinking areas, lowlands, and bore areas, and when the flow rate increases during rainfall, the sewage power increases, causing the sediment to float and outflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200432978-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, the sewage for the excess capacity of the first accommodation chamber 110 of the sewage introduced into the inlet 112 of the first accommodation chamber 110 is connected to the stream through the second accommodation chamber 120 ( in addition to being discharged to 122, the sewage contained in the sewage is filtered by the contaminant treatment unit 200 and guided to be discharged through the discharge port 114 of the first accommodation chamber 110 connected to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200435493-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, the sewage for the excess capacity of the first accommodation chamber 110 of the sewage introduced into the inlet 112 of the first accommodation chamber 110 is connected to the stream through the second accommodation chamber 120 ( in addition to being discharged to 122, the sewage contained in the sewage is filtered by the contaminant treatment unit 200 and guided to be discharged through the discharge port 114 of the first accommodation chamber 110 connected to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101382006-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and the treated water from which the contaminants have been removed is discharged to a stream or an appeal through the treated water discharge pipe 12"}, {"pat_id": "US-10322951-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the water with removed contaminant is drained from the drain pipe 54 disposed on the upstream side of the electrostatic filter 53 to the outside system"}, {"pat_id": "US-8211296-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the oxidizing chemical is preferably introduced into a zone of turbulent flow of the frac fluid through an eductor disposed upstream of the frac tanks, thereby achieving better mixing and better contact with the particular contaminant(s) then being treated"}, {"pat_id": "US-8226832-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the oxidizing chemical is preferably introduced into a zone of turbulent flow of the frac fluid through an eductor disposed upstream of the frac tanks, thereby achieving better mixing and better contact with the particular contaminant(s) then being treated"}, {"pat_id": "US-5562834-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the vaporized organic contaminants and steam removed from the top of the steam stripper are passed through a heat exchanger to raise the temperature of the stream to about 400 c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200432978-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, the sewage for the excess capacity of the first accommodation chamber 110 of the sewage introduced into the inlet 112 of the first accommodation chamber 110 is connected to the stream through the second accommodation chamber 120 ( in addition to being discharged to 122, the sewage contained in the sewage is filtered by the contaminant treatment unit 200 and guided to be discharged through the discharge port 114 of the first accommodation chamber 110 connected to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200435493-Y1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, the sewage for the excess capacity of the first accommodation chamber 110 of the sewage introduced into the inlet 112 of the first accommodation chamber 110 is connected to the stream through the second accommodation chamber 120 ( in addition to being discharged to 122, the sewage contained in the sewage is filtered by the contaminant treatment unit 200 and guided to be discharged through the discharge port 114 of the first accommodation chamber 110 connected to the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "US-8661819-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1, the steam energy conversion and power generation region 400 is also shown to include a first (e.g., upstream ) moisture-vapor separator 486 at an inlet side of the steam energy conversion device 410 to help reduce any moisture carry-over in the steam from the contaminant collection device 304"}, {"pat_id": "US-8776522-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1, the steam energy conversion and power generation region 400 is also shown to include a first (e.g., upstream ) moisture-vapor separator 486 at an inlet side of the steam energy conversion device 410 to help reduce any moisture carry-over in the steam from the contaminant collection device 304"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water waste stream is pumped through a cavitation nozzle, desirable effects occur which result in ionization of the water which causes oxidation of the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200402435-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, since the discharge point of the contaminated sewage cannot be accurately identified, the tracer is analyzed and traced back by analyzing the contaminant component of the sewage discharged into the stream.therefore, the main purpose of the present invention is to identify the cause of inflow of contaminated sewage or wastewater in the pipeline and to identify the location of the contaminated sewage or wastewater in the pipeline, and to identify the cause of the inflow of contaminated sewage and to take prompt action"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water waste stream is pumped through a cavitation nozzle, desirable effects occur which result in ionization of the water which causes oxidation of the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "US-9604157-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the extraction mechanism 100 functions to remove contaminants, such as water and solid particulates from a pumped gaseous stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-9604157-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the upstream force can be applied by the water mass on the sealing member 400 (e.g., in conjunction with gravity, centrifugal force, or another exterior force), by pressure generated by the pump 40, by built-up pressure due to the contaminants blocking the flow of pumped fluid 13 through the selection mechanism 300, or due to any other suitable force"}, {"pat_id": "US-9604157-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in response to the upstream force exceeding the threshold force, the sealing member 400 is preferably translated away from the first outlet 230 into the open mode, thereby unsealing the first outlet 230 and permitting contaminant flow from the extraction mechanism 100 into a second reservoir fluidly connected to the first outlet 230 (e.g., the ambient environment)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101802534-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, in the effluent stream, the sensor may indicate whether the concentration of a contaminant, such as a biologically tolerant compound, a biologically inhibitory compound, and / or a compound that is generally resistant to biodegradation, has reached a predetermined value or trend, value, or trend, so that the controller can be stimulated to perform some action upstream, downstream from, or at the sensor from the sensor"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the contaminant were lead (pb) in this example, the conductivity of the water would increase from about 200 \u03bcs/cm in the feed water stream to 2000 \u03bcs/cm in the waste water stream, which would significantly increase detection sensitivity and reduce measurement time of the contaminant sensor 175"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the contaminant sensor 175 is positioned in the waste water stream, the detection sensitivity of the contaminant sensor 175 is effectively increased compared to positioning it the feed water stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the readings of the contaminant sensor 175 are affected by the water quality (which includes the water s chemistry and other factors) of the waste water stream, and the water quality should be understood to properly deduce the concentration of contaminants in the feed water stream based on the readings of the contaminant sensor 175"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "additionally, by positioning the contaminant detection system 170 in the waste water stream where ions of contaminants are preconcentrated by the water treatment module 110, the effective sensitivity of the contaminant sensor 175 is increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100441620-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "air generating means installed at the lowermost lower portion of the contact layer to increase the dissolved oxygen concentration of the stream water flowing into the reaction tank and to generate air bubbles so that contaminants between the contact layers fall off"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101382006-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the present invention separates the overflow water and contaminants contained in the rainwater using the purification treatment tank 10, and the remaining water in the purification treatment tank 10 through the residual water discharge device 50, the remaining water treatment tank 60 ), and is configured to separate the contaminants contained in the residual water through the residual water treatment tank 60 to discharge to the stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-7531096-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such pre-treatment can cost effectively reduce the amount of organic contaminants prior to downstream reduction of organic contaminants (discussed below) cooling tower blowdown 30 exits feed tank 50 and is input into an evaporator system 52"}, {"pat_id": "US-8211296-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the oxidizing chemical is preferably introduced into a zone of turbulent flow of the frac fluid through an eductor disposed upstream of the frac tanks, thereby achieving better mixing and better contact with the particular contaminant(s) then being treated"}, {"pat_id": "US-8226832-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the oxidizing chemical is preferably introduced into a zone of turbulent flow of the frac fluid through an eductor disposed upstream of the frac tanks, thereby achieving better mixing and better contact with the particular contaminant(s) then being treated"}, {"pat_id": "US-11780746-B2", "para_id": "para_23", "text": "in step (a) the removal of pfas is undertaken by actively aerating the contaminated waste comprising pfas in a first vessel (110) to produce a waste stream (112) comprising a concentration of pfas and a first liquid stream (114) having at least some of the first group of contaminants"}]</data>
