  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-10981818-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the higher wattage and overcapacity of the heating element is preferred to ensure that the chamber temperature is maintained because the air pump would bring in cold air in very cold or freezing weather"}, {"pat_id": "US-4236382-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in any of the vacuum freezing processes described, an aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "US-5059228-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "referring to the processing of an aqueous solution by any vacuum freezing process, the aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "US-5080704-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "referring to the processing of an aqueous solution by any vacuum freezing process, the aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "US-5448892-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "vacuum freezing processes referring to the processing of an aqueous solution by any vacuum freezing process, the aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the heater 610 of the heater unit 600 is disposed in the conduit 510 as in one embodiment of the present invention, the heater 610 is directly in contact with the fire water in the conduit 510, and the heater 610 can directly heat the fire water in the conduit 510, the heating efficiency and energy utilization efficiency of the fire water in the conduit 510 is excellent, thereby freezing the fire water in the conduit 510 quickly it can be heated to the above temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the heater unit 600 and the water temperature detection unit 700 are both electrically connected to the control unit 800, and when the temperature of the fire water in the pipeline 510 sensed by the water temperature detection unit 700 is below the freezing point, the control unit 800 ) provides power to the heater unit 600 to directly supply heat to the fire hydrant 540 and the fire fighting water in the conduit 510 to prevent freezing due to freezing of the conduit 510"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "based on the temperature and flow of the fluid, the control system 1140 determines whether the fluid in the fluid conduit system 1102 is close to freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "based on the temperature and flow of the fluid, the control system 1230 determines whether the fluid in the fluid conduit system 1102 is close to freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "furthermore, each of those devices are actuated in response to ambient air temperature and thus will serve to trickle water when the air temperature is near the freezing temperature of water, even though the temperature of the water in the conduit may be at a higher temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the actuation of the unit depends upon the water temperature within the conduit, the unit will only operate to trickle water when there exists a real danger that freezing may occur, thus minimizing water waste"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when freezing temperatures are sensed by the bulb, there is an outflow of water from the valve device and an inflow of water from the inlet conduit, thereby preventing freezing of water within the tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4936114-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "sufficient aqueous ice slurry is fed to mixing tank 22 by conduit 54 to keep the temperature of the liquid therein close to, but above, the freezing point so that there is no increase in ice particle formation"}, {"pat_id": "US-7497228-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "because the temperature control valve measured a higher temperature, it would remain closed and not allow warmer water from below ground to replace the freezing water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, in one winter, a low temperature can cause freezing of a water pipe that supplies water from a water reservoir to a drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to this aspect of the present invention, the water supply control device checks the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor and intermittently drives the pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe supplying water to the water tank of the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101145007-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "water remaining inside the floating tube is automatically drained to the outside through the drain hole, which prevents the freezing and freezing of water at low temperature in winter because (can cause) there is no water remaining in the floating tube"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102572857-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another method for preventing the water pipe from freezing is to prevent the water pipe from freezing by artificially opening a water valve to continuously drain the water when it is expected that the water contained in the water pipe will freeze due to low temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200498205-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in the winter, if the permeated water that seeps into the pavement layer of the bridge deck is not drained quickly and remains, it freezes due to the low temperature, causing freezing and rupture of the pavement layer"}, {"pat_id": "US-4313452-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the lower end of the exterior thaw tube 32 thus thaws quickly and also freezes quickly, which provides a fast refreezing of the apparatus and reopening of the drain opening 30 should the ambient temperature, after only a short period of thaw, again go below freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the valve closing element of this patent is caused to open said valve and allow the drainage of fluid from a connected pipe in response to temperatures approaching the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is thus seen that it would be desirable to have a simple, inexpensive system for draining water lines at the approach of freezing temperatures, and in which the activating mechanism is maintained out of contact with the fluid both during and after its activation"}, {"pat_id": "US-6763845-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus a subject water utilizing device (e.g., an evaporative cooler and its associated piping system) and certain freezing temperature exposed-portions of applicant s device are drained and thus winterized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the heater unit 600 and the water temperature detection unit 700 are both electrically connected to the control unit 800, and when the temperature of the fire water in the pipeline 510 sensed by the water temperature detection unit 700 is below the freezing point, the control unit 800 ) provides power to the heater unit 600 to directly supply heat to the fire hydrant 540 and the fire fighting water in the conduit 510 to prevent freezing due to freezing of the conduit 510"}, {"pat_id": "US-6237620-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "which may require removal of a structural component of the mobile home, boat/yacht, cottage, or lodge, in order to provide access to the freeze damaged length of pipe or the particular fitting adversely affected by the freezing temperature in the winter months"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101404540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when there is a risk of freezing of the water meter m due to a drop in winter temperature and a rapid drop in the temperature of the tap water, the temperature of the heating wire w can be detected from the temperature information detected by the temperature sensor 100 and the flow rate information detected by the flow sensor 200, or not"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0008176-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the water is drawn off at the water temperature prevailing in the receptacle, the addition of that water to the flow through the heat exchanger in which the waste water gives off heat does not result in any cooling of this flow with the above- mentioned concomitant disadvantages and risks of freezing in the heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0354914-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "installations of water-air heat exchangers of different kinds, heat batteries in air conditioning equipment, ordinary water radiators etc often have problems with pipe ruptures due to freezing in low air temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "US-4838039-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "direct contact heat transfer requires less temperature difference between the vaporizing refrigerant and freezing solution than does indirect heat transfer systems to achieve the same energy transfer due to the elimination of the heat exchanger surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100912781-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "seventh, since the heating wire is provided on the outer surface of the body of the inlet and the dehydration unit, it is possible to prevent the viscosity rise and freezing of the slurry due to the temperature drop, and thus can be used to operate even in winter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101720174-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore, water passing through the first inlet 111 is relatively low in temperature immediately before freezing (hereinafter referred to as quot"}, {"pat_id": "US-10246349-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "however, the salinity of salt water/industrial brine 202 that enters freezing desalination cell/unit enclosure 271 via salt water/industrial brine inlet 275 also has influence on the freezing process (the higher the salt concentration, the lower the necessary freezing temperature to be accomplished)"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when freezing temperatures are sensed by the bulb, there is an outflow of water from the valve device and an inflow of water from the inlet conduit, thereby preventing freezing of water within the tank"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3706682-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[0069] (7) the first, second, and third short line cords are power cords, but instead, the first, second, and third short line cords themselves are self-temperature-controlled tropics t since the shape joint can be heated sufficiently by the connector itself, the effect of preventing freezing becomes more remarkable"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3706683-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[0064] (5) the first, second, and third short wire cords are power cords, but instead, the first, second, and third short wire cords themselves are self-temperature-controlled tropics t since the shape joint can be heated sufficiently by the connector itself, the effect of preventing freezing becomes more remarkable"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200307663-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "to solve the problem of excessive input of metering manpower and metering time due to the use of meter box and freezing of water meter which is easy to occur due to external temperature drop, the function was improved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the heater unit 600 serves to prevent damage to the pipeline 510 due to volume expansion caused by freezing and freezing of the fire fighting water in the pipeline 510 due to the influence of low temperature in the winter season"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the heater unit 600 and the water temperature detection unit 700 are both electrically connected to the control unit 800, and when the temperature of the fire water in the pipeline 510 sensed by the water temperature detection unit 700 is below the freezing point, the control unit 800 ) provides power to the heater unit 600 to directly supply heat to the fire hydrant 540 and the fire fighting water in the conduit 510 to prevent freezing due to freezing of the conduit 510"}, {"pat_id": "US-10634284-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, curves in the pipeline may tend to accumulate more solidified process fluid compared to straight sections of the pipeline, and anchor points along the pipeline may accumulate more solidified process fluid as a result of heat transfer to the anchors supporting the pipeline, which may drop the temperature of the anchor points below the freezing point of the process fluid"}, {"pat_id": "US-11047115-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it should be appreciated that if water temperatures are detected as being close to or below freezing, a pressure sensor may look for an increase in pipe pressure that may indicate freezing water in the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100634761-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when it is determined that the communication state is good, the temperature data of the water tank together with the ambient temperature data (which can determine the possibility of freezing of the water pipe, measured by the temperature sensor) and (if the pump abnormality can be determined) preferably, a current sensor is further provided to control the pump using the current data supplied to the pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to this aspect of the present invention, the water supply control device checks the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor and intermittently drives the pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe supplying water to the water tank of the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the outside air temperature falls below the reference value through the temperature sensor 270, the water supply control device 200 intermittently drives the pump 220 to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe 230"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200433469-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "control setting part the present invention relates to a simple abnormality of water, and more specifically, when the ambient temperature drops below 0 c and there is a possibility of freezing of water pipes, a water intake pump that drives water from underground pipes and the like is driven for a predetermined time interval"}, {"pat_id": "US-10981818-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the higher wattage and overcapacity of the heating element is preferred to ensure that the chamber temperature is maintained because the air pump would bring in cold air in very cold or freezing weather"}, {"pat_id": "US-4243522-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and 6 p.m., it is possible to use the waste water as a source of heat for a heat pump, the temperature of the waste water being sufficiently high that it can be reduced, such as by 5 c., without a risk of freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature of the water in the storage tank falls below a specified temperature for a specified period of time, thereby indicating that the possibility of freezing exists, the microprocessor activates the pump to dump water from the storage tank through the alternate outlet to the alternate destination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, in one winter, a low temperature can cause freezing of a water pipe that supplies water from a water reservoir to a drain"}, {"pat_id": "US-4018682-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in a practical sense, sludge from a retention pond is treated by the method of the present invention during the winter months of the year when the ambient temperature is below freezing at least part of the time, thereby foregoing the need to artificially freeze the water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "temperature sensor 38 is used to collect real-time temperature data and monitor the temperature of the incoming water to determine if conditions are conducive to pipe freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100385568-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this case, in the case of groundwater, after the operation of the temperature sensor 80 that detects the freezing temperature due to the characteristics of the groundwater, the water temperature (0) or more), it is preferable to have a timer to stop the continuous operation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100634761-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when it is determined that the communication state is good, the temperature data of the water tank together with the ambient temperature data (which can determine the possibility of freezing of the water pipe, measured by the temperature sensor) and (if the pump abnormality can be determined) preferably, a current sensor is further provided to control the pump using the current data supplied to the pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100643176-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is configured to prevent the phenomenon from occurring, and to prevent freezing and condensation due to the temperature difference between the temperature inside the sensor unit 52 and the sample when measuring the sample in a low temperature state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to this aspect of the present invention, the water supply control device checks the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor and intermittently drives the pump to prevent 