404-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "therefore, when the temperature drops, such as in the winter, freezing due to residual water inside the flow path is inevitable, and when freezing occurs, the entire water angle valve must be replaced, which inevitably results in excessive costs"}, {"pat_id": "US-11066813-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature drops, the system opens the main valve and allows the water to flow, thus preventing the pipe from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-4456024-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "ambient temperatures below freezing but of insufficient duration to reduce the water temperature to the freezing point, will not activate the valve resulting in an unnecessary discharge of water"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the valve closing element of this patent is caused to open said valve and allow the drainage of fluid from a connected pipe in response to temperatures approaching the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is therefore seen that the present invention provides a simple device for activating a fluid valve in response to a thermal, and specifically, to a freezing, change in temperature, without the requirement for external power or human intervention"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after the valve has been opened to bleed water from the water line, it thereafter closes because (cause) of such heat transfer and is again in position to operate responsively to freezing ambient temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when freezing temperatures are sensed by the bulb, there is an outflow of water from the valve device and an inflow of water from the inlet conduit, thereby preventing freezing of water within the tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, there is a need for a completely failure-safe freeze prevention valve that is useful under industrial conditions, automa