  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-4236974-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the oxidation and hence the rise in temperature mostly take place in mixing chamber 64, because that is where most of the impurities are burned"}, {"pat_id": "US-5571424-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, such calculations are first performed to determine the quantity and temperature of the hot water from central chamber 310 needed to heat the aqueous waste and oxidant in the inner annular chamber 335 to a temperature such that oxidation reaction can begin in the inner annular chamber"}, {"pat_id": "US-6121179-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus the input stream may preferably be heated to above the oxidation reaction ignition temperature without substantial heat exchange with an external source of heat--that is, without substantial heat exchange with other fluids via a heat exchanger, fired heater, or the like"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0595858-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the reaction mixture is heated within inlet end 16 to elevate the temperature of the reaction mixture and thereby increase the rate of oxidation of the reaction mixture"}, {"pat_id": "US-5106513-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "table 3 ______________________________________ effect of alkali on coal/ipa oxidation no alkali alkali ______________________________________ reactor inlet concentration, mg/kg coal 8900 10700 ipa 6700 6700 added naoh 0 290 1st stage reactor temperature, c"}, {"pat_id": "US-5470481-A", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "the reaction mixture is heated within inlet end 116 to elevate the temperature of the reaction mixture and thereby increase the rate of oxidation of the reaction mixture"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101044701-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, there is an urgent need to introduce a structure that can effectively absorb such heat deformation to protect the gravity wet oxidation reactor.the present invention created to solve the above problems is to protect the gravity wet oxidation reactor by effectively absorbing the heat deformation according to the temperature inside the gravity pressure vessel"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3672455-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, since the activity of iron bacteria, that is, the oxidation amount of iron may change due to the influence of temperature, the measuring tank 10 is maintained at a temperature at which the activity of iron bacteria is stabilized by the temperature regulator 5"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3672455-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, since the activity of iron bacteria, that is, the oxidation amount of iron may change due to the influence of temperature, the measuring tank 10 is maintained at a temperature at which the activity of iron bacteria is stabilized by the temperature regulator 5"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100735544-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "concentration of the high concentration of organic wastewater in the high temperature aerobic digestion tank (1a) is 2.5% 5% of the suitable solids, if the concentration of the solid is too low, the conditions that can be activated because the lack of energy sources for high temperature aerobic microorganisms it has a problem of generating insufficient heat of oxidation to form"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100953075-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, latent heat is scattered with water vapor during the dropping to evaporate the organic oxidation heat and the denitrification heat, and the temperature of the microorganism activity of the oxidizing tank is changed to the atmospheric temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101265963-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "comprising an apparatus for maintaining a reaction temperature in an aerobic tank, and forming an optimum reaction condition in the aerobic tank even with an external temperature change, thereby improving the efficiency of organic matter oxidation and nitrification and thereby stable discharge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101642081-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, even when only the oxidizing agent is supplied to the regeneration wastewater purification tank 140 during purification of regeneration wastewater, on the other hand, if the temperature of the regeneration wastewater is lower than the reference temperature, the oxidizing efficiency of the oxidizing agent is lowered, so that it is required to supply the reaction catalyst for promoting the oxidation reaction in addition to the oxidizing agent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "maintaining the temperature of the purified water flowing into and stored in the purified water tank unit 1100 by the anti-freezing heater unit 1600 at any one temperature selected from the range of 27 to 75 degrees celsius is to promote the activation of the advanced oxidation process (aop)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1661864-B1", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "in the method (1) in which the surface oxidation layer is formed in the gas phase, a mixed gas of a nitrogen gas and a small amount of air is introduced into a reaction vessel at a low temperature to oxidize \u03b1-fe present in the surface of the iron particles, thereby obtaining iron composite particles having a surface oxidation layer composed of fe3o4"}, {"pat_id": "US-5100560-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this oxidation method, the waste material is pressurized and fed into a reactor vessel along with compressed oxidant, either oxygen, air or oxygen-enriched air, and maintained therein under supercritical temperature conditions, that is at a temperature above 374 c., and, elevated pressure, to cause rapid oxidation"}, {"pat_id": "US-5106513-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "while supercritical water oxidation requires a thicker walled vessel due to higher operating pressure, the less dense process stream in supercritical temperature water oxidation necessitates a larger vessel to achieve a comparable residence time"}]</data>
</edge>
