  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-102883227-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "increasing the temperature of the wastewater passing through the cavitation generating device, and introducing the wastewater with the increased temperature into the lower part of a first-stage impeller"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102809593-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, cavitation occurs when the pressure of the water flowing inside the pump becomes lower than the saturated vapor pressure of the water at that temperature and pressure, causing partial vaporization of the water, creating bubbles"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102883227-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "a wastewater storage facility where wastewater containing ammonia is stored, a cavitation generating device that receives wastewater discharged from the above wastewater storage tank and generates cavitation to increase the temperature of wastewater containing ammonia"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102896533-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "and an ultrasonic water purification unit installed on the other side of the ultrasonic vibration unit to generate a cavitation effect, thereby providing high temperature, high pressure, and nano-bubble effects to the sterilization water"}]</data>
</edge>
