  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-0576981-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the sensor 51 also gives the possibility that when the water level in the washing chamber 21 drops, for example due to leakage losses, the vacuum blower 36 can be switched on again in order to compensate for these leakage losses and to always have a fully filled washing chamber available for washing processes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200428182-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "5 does not form a conduit in the main body because the motor is installed outside, and in addition to the water level measurement tube 220, a separate tube is not formed in order to prevent leakage of pressure from the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101729735-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to the coupling structure of the watertight packer 325, the water level is raised through the tubular packer 320, and the leakage of the sewage can be completely blocked"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399563-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the remote terminal device can determine and monitor the leakage of hazardous chemicals or the discharge of wastewater in the factory based on the gate status information and the water level information of the manhole water level sensor to be described later"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "leakage monitoring calculation processing for comparing the actual water level on the day of water leakage monitoring with the water leakage occurrence water level pattern and comparing the actual water level on the day of water leakage monitoring with the water level upper limit (allowable) pattern or the water level lower limit (allowable) pattern and when the actual water level exceeds the water leakage occurrence water level pattern, it is determined that water leakage has occurred due to a break in the water pipeline , and the actual water level exceeds the water level upper limit (allowable) pattern or the water level lower limit (allowable) pattern"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "as a result, the reliability of controlling the water level of the water tank can be improved, and there is an advantage that the control device does not malfunction by another even if an error occurs in any one of the pressure sensor and the angle sensor such as leakage into the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range, it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank, and also, if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor, such as leakage into the water pipe, the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4297310-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[0022] reservoir water level abnormal drop monitoring is intended to detect a sudden drop in the water level of a reservoir due to water leakage due to a distribution pipe accident or a large amount of water discharge due to a fire"}, {"pat_id": "JP-H0641138-Y2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "next, when running water is generated in the pipe 2 due to a leakage accident or the like, it rises above the overflow water level 10 in the water reservoir 8"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0576981-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the sensor 51 also gives the possibility that when the water level in the washing chamber 21 drops, for example due to leakage losses, the vacuum blower 36 can be switched on again in order to compensate for these leakage losses and to always have a fully filled washing chamber available for washing processes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "as a result, the reliability of controlling the water level of the water tank can be improved, and there is an advantage that the control device does not malfunction by another even if an error occurs in any one of the pressure sensor and the angle sensor such as leakage into the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range, it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank, and also, if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor, such as leakage into the water pipe, the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101114764-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, there are advantages in that various accidents such as fire and water leakage, which may be caused by malfunction of the water level sensor, may be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399563-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the remote terminal device can determine and monitor the leakage of hazardous chemicals or the discharge of wastewater in the factory based on the gate status information and the water level information of the manhole water level sensor to be described later"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is no local precipitation, but that there are water levels above a threshold, the control system 100 may track property operations to determine if there is a problematic operation that may be causing water leakage within the property"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6492150-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "that is, the circuit for detecting the conduction between the electrodes due to the water leakage is designed using the circuit for detecting the water level of the water receiving tank conventionally used"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "as a result, the reliability of controlling the water level of the water tank can be improved, and there is an advantage that the control device does not malfunction by another even if an error occurs in any one of the pressure sensor and the angle sensor such as leakage into the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range, it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank, and also, if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor, such as leakage into the water pipe, the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101676999-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore, according to the present invention, it is possible to monitor the state of water leakage or foreign matter introduced into the water tank 1 by monitoring the rapid change of the water level and the water quality, thereby enabling cleaner and safer water quality management"}, {"pat_id": "US-4709723-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "during periods of high ground water levels, this leakage enabled additional fluid to flow into the tank to compensate for the increased hydraulic pressure of surrounding ground water and water saturated soil"}]</data>
