  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-7774358-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "when the water level becomes abnormal (rising), factors such as blockage of the discharge pipe, backflow from the discharge pipe (rainwater, etc.), failure of the discharge pump, or blockage of the return pipe 25 cause the water level to rise from the normal water level, causing the floating body 1 to tilt more"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0211164-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "if both yes signals are present at the and gate 41 at the same time, then there is a blockage in the drain pipe 13, because otherwise the flow through the drain pipe 13 would be significantly greater at such high water levels and there will therefore be a fault message indicating this blockage reports, and / or triggered a security process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841664-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101054375-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet port 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20 increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102599308-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in cases where the drainage function is lost due to blockage by various foreign substances, rainwater whose water level rises due to poor drainage treatment can be safely bypassed and treated to prevent flooding damage due to rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it relates to a pipe blockage prediction system, a central control system that can predict the possibility of blockage in each section of the pipe by measuring the water level in each section