ated in the land stream flows into the sea"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, it has a significant effect of fundamentally blocking the red tide phenomenon that occurs when polluted river water from rivers on land flows into the sea"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the reason why the structure of the above control unit (99999) is configured in a shape to block both the front and rear passages is that it is a structure to fundamentally block the phenomenon in which sand and gravel accumulate in the front and rear passages due to gravity when river water overflows, thereby losing the bottom water discharge function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102898667-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "additionally, it has a significant effect of fundamentally blocking the red tide phenomenon that occurs when polluted river water from rivers on land flows into the sea"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100607882-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the sewage from which the chemical is removed passes through the carbon block 7 and passes through the cover 11 and is discharged to the river through the drain 5 formed lower than the height of the filter box 6"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200420164-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to the blocking, there is an effect of preventing the backflow of the river to the drain pipe of the sewage pipe simply and conveniently"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200480951-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in case of overflowing the river, and the sewage inlet is closed, thereby blocking some of the backwash of the sewage"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4570636-B2", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in order to further reduce the momentum of the water flowing into the river water reservoir 2 through the dewatering pond 7, a concrete speed reducing block 8 is installed between the river water reservoir 2 and the diversion reservoir 7"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4570636-B2", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "as a result, the energy of the flowing water when colliding with the resin skeleton block 11 in the river water reservoir 2 is further reduced, and the water storage space formed by the resin skeleton block 11 of the river water reservoir 2 is less likely to be damaged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, in order to prepare for the water shortage situation, there are ways to minimize the problems of securing the water by blocking the above-mentioned large artificial dam, reservoir or river water, and to secure the water that is insufficient without performing relatively large construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518747-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the shore protection block of the present invention can be installed in a lake, a dam reservoir slope, a river, or a ditch to provide a space where various aquatic plants, aquatic insects and fish can coexist along with water purification.10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102290035-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in the prior art, even if a fire-fighting helicopter wants to be supplied with fire-fighting water from a river, lake, or reservoir, the suction hose of the fire-fighting helicopter is blocked due to numerous floating objects in or on the water"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4037065-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[0023] in block b2, information on the water quality in the lake, aquatic organisms, flow conditions from the river / lake information sensor 40, and the current and future predicted values of the inflow and water quality of the river / lake from block b1"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the water quality can be discharged only purified rainwater or clear rainwater has the effect of greatly improving the water quality of the river.1 is a block diagram of a rainwater storage device according to the present invention, 2 is a cross-sectional configuration diagram of a switch and a septic tank and a storage tank showing an initial excellent movement path accordin