er"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the pollutants deposited on the road surface are sequentially transported by road drainage due to rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the removal process of pollutants deposited on the road surface is almost completed in the initial rainfall stage, and since the amount of pollutants in the road drainage due to the subsequent rainfall remains small, the road drainage does not come into contact with the media installed in the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200358330-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, the road surface drainage treatment apparatus having an initial excellent filtration function according to the present invention has a road drainage capacity capable of smoothly draining the road drainage increased during rainfall, and is deposited on the road surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102010653-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, since sediments generated during rainfall are often removed automatically before being deposited in the settlement or reservoir, the settlement or reservoir can always maintain the efficiency of the design capacity"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100350735-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, during rainfall, the amount of sewage inflow is high and the flow rate is fast, so that the soil is not deposited in the sedimentation tank and flows into the dwelling house as it is, so that the cross section of the dwelling house 3 is reduced and the sewage terminal treatment plant is caused"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the removal process of pollutants deposited on the road surface is almost completed in the initial rainfall stage, and since the amount of pollutants in the road drainage due to the subsequent rainfall remains small, the road drainage does not come into contact with the media installed in the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200171293-Y1", "para_id"