  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101014995-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the amount of water increases, the water level sensor detects and opens the initial rainwater blocking door to remove the foreign matter from the primary strainer after collecting the rainwater from the primary strainer, filter it once more from the strainer, and then remove the foreign substance in the sedimentation chamber for final precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101039196-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this structure is to block the inflow of the initial excellent water when the internal water level of the first excellent soil chamber 21 and the second excellent soil chamber 31 is increased due to the continuous inflow of the initial excellent rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101215187-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the high water level alarm sensor 46 is a water level of the sewage and rainwater in the chamber 12 of the collecting facility 10 above the limit point because the sewage pipe 16 is not blocked in the rain due to a malfunction of the first water level detection sensor 42"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101258565-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater introduced into the rainwater chamber 10 is increased in quantity and gradually increased in water level to reach the moving induction plate 300 installed in the sewage inlet 22 and the blocking plate 260"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008617-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "at the end of the sewer pipe (1), the sewage discharge port (2) is normally closed to guide the sewage to the sewage treatment plant through the rainwater discharge chamber (3) to block the discharge of odors and to increase the amount of sewage into rainwater that flows during rainy weather"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102773372-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "seals the rainwater receiving chamber (420) with the buoyancy of the rainwater (c), thereby blocking the fluid inflow into the casing (100)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3466513-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the event that the rain overflow basin 1 is busy or there is a blockage in the area of the retaining element 8, the water can thus flow from the basin chamber 5 to the basin overflow 7 via the emergency overflow 16 without being cleaned"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784989-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in treating rainwater containing a large amount of turbidity, a blockage due to a large amount of turbidity may occur in the chamber portion 210 of the vortex valve, so that an outflow downstream from the rainwater discharge portion 130 of the manhole body may occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841267-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, in the conventional rainwater discharge chamber, the floating contaminants 5 flowing in do not flow into the collecting pipe 3 in rainy weather, but are discharged into the public water through the discharge pipe 4 so that water pollution of the public water is ) is the cause"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101926744-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the contaminants settled in the excellent water collecting chamber 11 lower the degree of purification of excellent purification, the water is guided to the contaminant discharge chamber 12 so as not to feed water to the purified water supply water chamber 14, which is conducted through the drain portion 16"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102055349-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, by simplifying the structure of the permeation ditches, the efficiency of rainwater discharge is increased, and at the same time, contaminants are removed from the pretreatment water, the irrigation chamber, and the ditches, etc"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3309310-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, contamination in the storage space can be effectively avoided by always takes place with sinking water level in the rain overflow basin, a backflow of water from the storage space to the pelvic chamber"}, {"pat_id": "US-11298635-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "alternative structures, for example, chambers filled with porous media and underdrains, can be cost prohibitive and may fail resulting in flooding the rain garden with debris, which requires extensive clean-up"}, {"pat_id": "US-8501016-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "alternative structures, for example, chambers filled with porous media and underdrains, can be cost prohibitive and may fail resulting in flooding the rain garden with debris, which requires extensive clean-up"}, {"pat_id": "US-11298635-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the storm water pretreatment chamber prevents premature rain garden bypass of the untreated storm water due to sediment and debris accumulation"}, {"pat_id": "US-8501016-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the storm water pretreatment chamber eliminates premature rain garden bypass of the untreated storm water due to sediment and debris accumulation"}, {"pat_id": "US-8501016-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the storm water pretreatment chamber eliminates premature rain garden bypass of the untreated storm water due to sediment and debris accumulation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the rainwater flowing on the road 28 in the direction of the arrow b in case of rainfall moves toward each grill 14 and passes through the pit chamber 16, the screening chamber 40, and the grit chamber 48, and then the leakage pipe 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102388770-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the inlet opening/closing plate 120 is submerged in a closed state of the upper inlet 11 due to the rainwater condition that does not require a closure, a free space provided between surrounding parts for smooth operation of the inlet opening/closing plate 120 rainwater may leak into the rainwater chamber 110 through such a method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102408952-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the inlet opening/closing plate 120 is submerged in a closed state of the upper inlet 111 due to a rainwater condition that does not require a closure, a free space provided between surrounding components for smooth operation of the inlet opening/closing plate 120 rainwater may leak into the rainwater chamber 110 through such a method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the rainwater flowing on the road 28 in the direction of the arrow b in case of rainfall moves toward each grill 14 and passes through the pit chamber 16, the screening chamber 40, and the grit chamber 48, and then the leakage pipe 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the rainwater collected in the pit chamber 16 reaches a level corresponding to the height of the connection hole 44, the rainwater moves from the pit chamber 16 toward the screening chamber 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the rainwater flowing on the road 28 in the direction of the arrow b in case of rainfall moves toward each grill 14 and passes through the pit chamber 16, the screening chamber 40, and the grit chamber 48, and then the leakage pipe 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and the wear 22 installed in the rainwater chamber 20 can be installed high enough because the flow rate can be adjusted by adjusting the water gate (70)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, if the height of the wear 22 is excessively increased, this may affect the inundation of the upstream superior rain chamber 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and the wear 22 installed in the rainwater chamber 20 can be installed high enough because the flow rate can be adjusted by adjusting the water gate (70)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, if the height of the wear 22 is excessively increased, this may affect the inundation of the upstream superior rain chamber 20"}]</data>
