  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101147332-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the existing dams and bore streams or rivers are blocked by concrete structures and used for water or power generation.however, there is an excessive amount of co 2 (0.9 ton per ton of cement) due to cement production and an ecosystem caused by heavy metals such as cr +8"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, in order to prepare for the water shortage situation, there are ways to minimize the problems of securing the water by blocking the above-mentioned large artificial dam, reservoir or river water, and to secure the water that is insufficient without performing relatively large construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518747-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the shore protection block of the present invention can be installed in a lake, a dam reservoir slope, a river, or a ditch to provide a space where various aquatic plants, aquatic insects and fish can coexist along with water purification.10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102187983-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in addition, it has a significant effect of fundamentally blocking the red tide phenomenon that occurs when contaminated river water generated in the land stream flows into the sea"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, it has a significant effect of fundamentally blocking the red tide phenomenon that occurs when polluted river water from rivers on land flows into the sea"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102817242-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the reason why the structure of the above control unit (99999) is configured in a shape to block both the front and rear passages is that it is a structure to fundamentally block the phenomenon in which sand and gravel accumulate in the front and rear passages due to gravity when river water overflows, thereby losing the bottom water discharge function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102898667-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "additionally, it has a significant effect of fundamentally blocking the red tide phenomenon that occurs when polluted river water from rivers on land flows into the sea"}]</data>
