  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-5322629-A", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "this is due to the continual accretion of pollutants on the drained surfaces over time"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "next, the gutter block 1 having the above structure the function and effect of (cause) the drainage tool 2 will be described"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the first conduit e1 or the second conduit e it is possible to guide rainwater and the like that have entered into the gutter block 1 through the drainage grooves 1d and 1d into the gutter block 1 without being blocked by the covering material w placed on the lid-hanging stepped portion 1b"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "wherein:it produces the effect of (cause) item 1.also, as described in claim 12.according to the gutter block provided with the drainage tool, the effect of claim 5 is obtained.play the fruit"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "further, according to the gutter block provided with the drainage device described in claim 13 , in addition to the effect of (cause) claim 11 or 12 , rainwater and the like that have entered the first water conduit can be along the lower surface that is the inclined surface"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100435535-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the conventional sidewalk block has a problem that the flooding area occurs frequently in the case where the drainage is vulnerable because (cause) the phenomenon that the rain water is not submerged through the ground of the block and concentrated in the sewer pipe occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100593258-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in the boundary block system capable of drainage, installed between the sidewalks and the driveway, the wheels of the vehicle are removed to serve as a boundary between the sidewalks and the roadway, to drain the rainwater on the roadway, and to prevent the vehicle from rushing to the sidewalk due to the collision with the car"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100593258-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "still another object of the present invention is to provide a boundary block system that is easy to clean the drainage path and that can substantially increase the running area of the vehicle"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100633532-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, if rainwater and sewage flowing into the rainwater receiver 51 contain foreign matters, the rainwater and sewage introduced into the lower portion due to the foreign matters are blocked, and the rainwater and sewage are not drained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100649520-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, due to this, various kinds of sediment are introduced into and stacked in the manhole, and the accumulated sediment may be introduced into the sewage pipe again to block or narrow the sewage pipe, causing problems in drainage of sewage water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100649520-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is because (cause) the foreign matter is moved through the sewage canal 40, along with the sewage and sewage in several directions, so that the foreign matter is accumulated in the sewer 60 to block or narrow the sewer pipe so that the problem does not occur in the drainage of the sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100710632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, in order to prevent the backflow of the odor, the vinyl bag may be covered on the grating of the drain, but in case of sudden rain, the plastic bag may block the drain of the rainwater, which may prevent the rainwater from draining and cause a safety accident due to the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100720157-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "still another object of the present invention is to provide a odor prevention manhole that can catch filth flowing into the manhole, thereby blocking the source of odor, and preventing clogging of the drain hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100720398-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "it is possible to secure the strength, and because (cause) the drain pipe is normally blocked by the odor backflow installed in the drain pipe, it is possible to block the odor backflow from the sewage main pipe to the rainwater receiving side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781488-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to prevent the drainage block 2 from being pressed down due to the load of the vehicle while forming a part of the road 1 together with the drainage blocks 2 arranged as above, the mutually arranged drainage blocks 2 are provided"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781488-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the upper edge of the drainage passage 2a of the drainage block 2 is formed in a sharp shape, since the shape of the drainage passage 2a may be easily broken due to the impact of driving of the vehicle, the drainage passage of the drainage block 2a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100913911-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and maintain a fixed state (odor blocking state), but the backflow allowable plate 50 is in close contact with the lower shielding plate 40 due to the water pressure of the backflow water flowing into the drainage space 41 of the lower shielding plate 40 the backflow allowance plate 50 which was in contact with the part 53 is rotated upward, and the inflow backflow water is smoothly flowed back while being drained through the central drain port 64"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101054283-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the drain pipe is prevented from being blocked by the foreign matter deposited on the bottom of the manhole, thereby making it possible to smoothly drain the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101124407-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result (lead to), the blocking plate 24 blocking the drain hole 11a can prevent the pests such as mosquitoes grown in the sewage pipe from spreading to the outside while reducing the discharge of odors in the sewage pipe to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133441-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the blocking plate opening and closing member 130 stops the inflow of rainwater into the rainwater tank 132 after the rain, rainwater is drained into the drain hole 132 formed in the rainwater tank 132 to reduce (becoming) the amount of rainwater in the rainwater tank 132"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101178211-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, when a large amount of water is instantaneously blocked due to a foreign object such as fallen leaves or a large amount of water due to a heavy rain or heavy rain, various foreign substances that are swept away with the water are disposed on the upper part of the drain cover"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101178211-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention is to block the upper surface of the drain cover due to foreign matters, or in particular, even when a large amount of water in a moment of heavy rain or heavy rains can be drained smoothly without clogging with foreign matter, so that the water around the drain cover it not only prevents seizing but also provides excellent effects to prevent flooding and the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101189539-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, if the wastes flowing with the sewage flow into the tea house, or if more earth and sand are introduced into the tea house due to many rainwater, garbage and soil will accumulate in the tea house, which will block or drain the tea house"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a media plate formed in a mat shape having a predetermined size such that the drain blocks are stacked at a predetermined thickness on the stacked upper portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101208359-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is because (cause) the blocking plate is not completely covered by the safety net may leak odor from the drain pipe, there is a problem that rainwater or sewage is not easily discharged by the interference of the float while the float floats to a certain height"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101229485-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, when a large amount of water is instantaneously blocked due to a foreign object such as fallen leaves or a large amount of water due to a heavy rain or heavy rain, various foreign substances that are swept away with the water are disposed on the upper part of the drain cover"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101275666-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "formed at the bottom of the sump (1) after the accumulation, the discharge pipe 2 has a structure that is discharged through the drain pipe 2, thereby becoming a main factor to block the drain pipe (2)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101275666-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the present invention can effectively block various kinds of contaminants such as soil and leaves by installing a separate strainer inside the sump, thereby preventing the blockage of the drain pipe in advance and at the same time improving the drainage efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101387770-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when using spherical ceramic materials for acid mine drainage treatment, it is expected to prevent the blockage of reactor and coating of neutralizer due to sediment during long-term use, which is the biggest problem in existing acid mine drainage treatment facilities"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101400313-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the lifting cylinder 63 is lifted by the buoyancy caused by the constant, so that the stopper 59 blocks the drain hole 49a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518865-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by providing the guide block 66 on the upper side of the drainage passage 52, rainwater that suddenly overflows due to heavy rainfall or the like is prevented, so that flooding of the earths due to heavy rainfall can be stably prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519076-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is another object of the present invention to provide drainage and cleaning of an inner section which is clogged due to accumulation of gravels that move along rainwater flowing due to long-term use of the drainage pipe embedded in the slope of the block"}, {"