  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "specifically, when the water level gauge 111 detects that the water level in the contaminant removal tank 110 is higher than the specified water level, control is performed to relatively increase the amount of water transferred by the advection pump 122, and the contamination level is also increased"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "for example, in the case of the water level gauge 111 having a configuration in which an on signal is output when the water level of the contaminant removal tank 110 exceeds a prescribed water level defined in advance and an off signal is outputted when the water level falls below the prescribed water level, the amount of effluent water can be derived from the time when the off signal switches"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the pressure gauge detects and measures the pressure caused by the initial excellent or sediment contaminants in the initial excellent treatment facility 1, and performs the detection step, and the level gauge detects the initial excellent water level in the initial excellent treatment facility 1 the measurement is performed to detect"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "specifically, when the water level gauge 111 detects that the water level in the contaminant removal tank 110 is higher than the specified water level, control is performed to relatively increase the amount of water transferred by the advection pump 122, and the contamination level is also increased"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7709393-B2", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in the present invention, the water level gauge 300 is preferably a non-contact type, and more preferably an ultrasonic type, from the viewpoint of the risk of false detection due to contamination of the sensor unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200201276-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the magnitude of the signal sensed and output by the strain gauge 31 is to set the deformation value of the strain gauge 31 due to the buoyancy of the buoy 35 for the high and low water level at the time of installing the automatic water level controller"}]</data>
