  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100614939-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention, by installing a buoyancy blocking device 130 is operated by buoyancy during the sewage backflow on the bottom surface of the rainwater inlet 113 of the manhole 110 to block the inlet 113, the rainwater from the original while performing the function of, the guerrilla torrential rain, flooding due to the backflow of sewage due to the flood effect is to be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100704901-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in the present invention, the rainwater blocking device 200 is the body portion 210 and the inlet port 212 formed in the body portion 210 to form an overall shape, the rain discharged from the outside primarily the first outlet 220 to send to the rainwater stabilization zone 120, and the secondary outlet 230 to discharge the rainwater introduced from the second to the rainwater storage zone 170 and the outside it includes a third outlet 240 to discharge the rainwater introduced to the third discharge to the rainwater discharge zone 180"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100779513-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the amount of rainwater flowing through the inlet 610 is large, as the main cartridge 620 and the auxiliary cartridge 630 are suspended, the extension part of the water gate 60 accommodated in the receiving groove 74 ( 64 is also moved upward to block the bottom discharge port 73 of the waterproof wall (70)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101258565-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is preferable that the area of the blocking plate 260 is made larger than the wastewater inlet 22 and the opening 110 to control the inflow of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101258565-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater introduced into the rainwater chamber 10 is increased in quantity and gradually increased in water level to reach the moving induction plate 300 installed in the sewage inlet 22 and the blocking plate 260"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is because the sediment contained in the initial rainwater is mainly deposited on the bottom of the block close to the inlet 1, so that the washing water is advantageously discharged in a direction opposite to the flow direction when the rainwater is supplied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399564-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the gate 20 not only collects an appropriate amount of sewage or rainwater by opening and closing the inlet, but also blocks the pressure from being transmitted into the collecting pipe due to the rise of the water level in the conduit during flooding to prevent damage to the collecting pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102476350-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result (lead to), in a state where the opening and closing door 112 blocks the opening 111a of the upper cover 111, it is possible to thoroughly block the odor of sewage from leaking out through the rainwater inlet 111c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102476351-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result (lead to), in a state where the opening and closing door 112 blocks the opening 111a of the upper cover 111, it is possible to thoroughly block the odor of sewage from leaking out through the rainwater inlet 111c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore, to block the inflow of rainwater into the wastewater storage tank (30), the above-described rainwater inflow prevention device (100) is installed in the middle of the wastewater inlet pipe (40)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102838013-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, especially in the rainy season or in the fall, foreign substances such as fallen leaves can block the inlet, making it difficult to drain, which can easily lead to flooding and human casualties"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102897725-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "flows in through the inlet (11), the rotation blocking plate (21) is pushed directly below the inlet (11) by the pressure or load generated, thereby allowing the inflow of sewage (1) or rainwater (2), etc., into the inlet (11)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102897725-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when there is no inflow of sewage (1) or rainwater (2), etc., the rotation blocking plate (21) moves along the inclination angle (a) to be positioned directly below the inlet (11), thereby enabling the blocking of the foul odor (3)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102897725-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this way, the present invention is installed on a manhole or grating to allow the smooth inflow of sewage and rain, etc., and when the inflow is complete, it naturally blocks the inlet without any additional work, thereby providing the effect of closely blocking the foul odors flowing out from below"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200312015-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if a backflow phenomenon of sewage occurs inside the catchment manhole in a low zone due to guerrilla heavy rain, the upper structure of the catchment manhole is configured to be lifted up to block the inlet of the barrier fastening frame"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200381089-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in case of rain, as the inflow of sewage increases, the frame plate is kept horizontal to block the sewage inlet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200403906-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in such a state, when rainwater flows instantaneously, when the rainwater is instantaneously introduced, the floats 40 are raised to block the inlet 12 of the buoy automatic shutoff valve body 10 due to the disk 20, and the sewage and rainwater are sewage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101089297-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the inner cylinder 142 is installed inside the inlet 122 to increase the flow rate of rainwater flowing into the contaminant collecting network 130, so that the contaminants mixed with rainwater (including the flocculents)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202677-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this, the rainwater introduced into the water collection tank 40 along the raw water inlet pipe 46 may include a contaminant and mud not filtered by the screen filter 20 described above, the bottom of the collecting tank 40 there is an effect of sinking by spraying in the down direction of the sump (40)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101261597-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the inflow of the fluid is small, all the fluid flowing into the second fluid inlet hole 22 can be introduced into the first fluid inlet hole 11 to go through the treatment process of contaminants, the fluid that does not flow into the first fluid inlet hole 11 may flow along the pipe to be drained to the drain pipe connector 23"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "subsequently, when the flow into the rainwater inlet pipe 5 is not smooth due to the contaminants introduced into the rainwater inlet 200 together with the rainwater, some of the rainwater flowing into the rainwater inlet 200 is the rainwater inlet 200"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101353045-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the second filter 400 is installed on the bottom surface of the filtration unit 3 of the housing 1 in a form surrounding the inlet of the outlet 20 to remove contaminants in the rainwater exiting through the outlet 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101375866-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, like the initial rainwater treatment device 100, the rainwater discharge reduction device 200 is a contaminant in the rainwater flowing through the rainwater inlet 250 and the rainwater inlet 250, the rainwater flows from the outside after filtering the filter may further include a filter net 260 to discharge the rainwater filtered to the vegetation filtration layer 210 side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101977695-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater on the road surface 1 flows through the inlet port 411 and falls to the upper side of the water permeable filter agent 493 to remove the contaminants adhering to the lower side of the screen net 492 and the water permeable filter agent 493 the drainage of the rainwater can be smoothly performed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102779569-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rain water inlet device with contaminant removal functionthe present invention relates to a rainwater collecting device having a contaminant removing function, and more specifically, to a rainwater collecting device having a contaminant removing function for preventing clogging of an internal passage due to foreign substances, thereby enabling rainwater to drain more smoothly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(2) since the filter which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is installed in the treatment tank, the drainage flowed into the inlet of the storm drain flows through the flow path including the maintenance tank and the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the water in the rainwater inlet space 12 filled with only clear rainwater may prevent contamination of the river even if it flows into the river through the rainwater discharge unit 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the protrusion (3) is the air is discharged through the air discharge portion 33, the rain is introduced from the rain inlet 121 by using stainless in the metal to prevent corrosion, such as rust due to rust"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the protrusions 3 may discharge air through the air discharge part 33 and use stainless steel among metals to prevent corrosion due to rust by rainwater flowing from the rainwater inlet 121"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and the protrusion 3 is in the inner space 31 through the air outlet 33 air is discharged, and it is preferable to use stainless steel among metals to prevent corrosion by rust due to inflow of rainwater from the rainwater inlet 121"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781790-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the protruding cylinder 21 is the air is discharged through the air outlet 211, it is preferable to use stainless steel in the metal to prevent the corrosion, such as rust due to the rain is introduced from the inlet (12)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200436180-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, the pipe for socket for sewage and drainage according to the present invention is formed in the socket even when a gap between the inlet and outlet and the socket occurs due to partial flow of the sewage and drainage or the pipe due to ground subsidence and external impact"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102388770-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the inlet opening/closing plate 120 is submerged in a closed state of the upper inlet 11 due to the rainwater condition that does not require a closure, a free space provided between surrounding parts for smooth operation of the inlet opening/closing plate 120 rainwater may leak into the rainwater chamber 110 through such a method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102408952-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the inlet opening/closing plate 120 is submerged in a closed state of the upper inlet 111 due to a rainwater condition that does not require a closure, a free space provided between surrounding components for smooth operation of the inlet opening/closing plate 120 rainwater may leak into the rainwater chamber 110 through such a method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200322595-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "there is considerable difficulty in construction because the inlet pipe connection part or outlet pipe connection part of the receiver does not match, and if the inlet pipe or outlet pipe which is already constructed is forcibly bent and connected to the rainwater receiver, the connection part is weak and easily leaks"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100420101-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a flow control valve having an integrally coaxially connected valve body capable of lifting up and down is accommodated inside the manhole cylinder, and the float rises due to a rise in the level of the rainwater introduced through the upper rainwater inlet pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200338729-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention was devised to solve the above problem, and the sediment reduces the drop of sewage from the inlet of the sewer, thereby minimizing the lifting of the sediment, thereby reducing the amount of drainage that can prevent the sediment from entering the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100968550-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the conventional non-point pollutant treatment device has a obstacle in generalization because it has a structure that is subject to topographical constraints such as poor filtration efficiency if there is no drop between the inlet and the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101218752-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the inlet part 21 may change the porosity and permeability coefficient according to the particle size of the aggregate used, and when the porosity and the permeability coefficient are increased, foreign matter may be included in the rainwater flowing into the collection pipe 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the protrusion (3) is the air is discharged through the air discharge portion 33, the rain is introduced from the rain inlet 121 by using stainless in the metal to prevent corrosion, such as rust due to rust"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the protrusions 3 may discharge air through the air discharge part 33 and use stainless steel among metals to prevent corrosion due to rust by rainwater flowing from the rainwater inlet 121"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and the protrusion 3 is in the inner space 31 through the air outlet 33 air is discharged, and it is preferable to use stainless steel among metals to prevent corrosion by rust due to inflow of rainwater from the rainwater inlet 121"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100781790-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "te