  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for reference, the rainwater discharge structure using a single pump (p) is difficult to achieve the normal rainwater discharge of the transfer pipe far from the pump due to the increase in the volume of the transfer pipe (p1) when the construction length of the storage block 10 is long"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200475713-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater in the block is usually removed by using a pneumatic pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200475713-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "most of the rainwater is removed through the siphon principle, and only the remaining rainwater is removed by the pneumatic pump in removing the rainwater accumulated in the hull block, etc., so that the rainwater can be quickly removed and the air consumption can be minimized"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7774358-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "when the water level becomes abnormal (rising), factors such as blockage of the discharge pipe, backflow from the discharge pipe (rainwater, etc.), failure of the discharge pump, or blockage of the return pipe 25 cause the water level to rise from the normal water level, causing the floating body 1 to tilt more"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the initial rainwater and sediment contaminants are completely excluded from the initial rainwater treatment facility 1 and the pressure or water level becomes zero, the drain pump 21 receiving the water is driven to operate the water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "due to the use of the pump, the rainwater channel and the dirty water channel 4 can be at any level to each other, i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101246202-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the water collecting groove 402 provides a volume for collecting water introduced into the concrete structure 400 due to leakage of water supply pipes or inflow of rainwater, and a worker is provided with a water pump (hereinafter, not shown) separately provided through the inspection opening 401"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200295999-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the purpose is to prevent the failure and wear of the submersible pump 60 due to frequent starting and stopping of the submersible pump 60 for use of rainwater in toilet water or landscape water, thereby prolonging its life"}]</data>
