  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "4a-b, the filtered seawater may be provided to a treatment block 260 and either sent through blend/bypass line 225 or pumped by variable speed high-pressure pump 212, which pushes the filtered seawater through to one or more membrane pressure vessels (e.g., 214, 216, and 218), thereby creating a permeate stream and a concentrate stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-10329171-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6a-b, a system and/or method of the present invention may be configured so that the variable speed high-pressure pump 212 pushes the filtered seawater 611 through one or more treatment blocks, thereby creating a concentrate stream 634 and a permeate stream (not shown)"}, {"pat_id": "US-10343118-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "4a-b, the filtered seawater may be provided to a treatment block 260 and either sent through blend/bypass line 225 or pumped by variable speed high-pressure pump 212, which pushes the filtered seawater through to one or more membrane pressure vessels (e.g., 214, 216, and 218), thereby creating a permeate stream and a concentrate stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-10343118-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6a-b, a system and/or method of the present invention may be configured so that the variable speed high-pressure pump 212 pushes the filtered seawater 611 through one or more treatment blocks, thereby creating a concentrate stream 634 and a permeate stream (not shown)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101171869-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the pumping of the stream water 2 collected in the sump 120 continues while the collection efficiency of the screen 110 is lowered due to the blockage of the lower bed 4, the water level in the sump 120 is increased"}, {"pat_id": "US-5314619-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(it is possible, but not desirable, to terminate pipe 26 short of a complete loop, such as just upstream of valve 25 and coupling 27, but this can lead to blockage and pressure problems.) the water from pump 54 is pumped into pipe 26 though a directional coupling 27, such as a 45 lateral, so that the water circulates in the direction shown by arrow 23"}, {"pat_id": "US-8857473-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the flexible hose is pushed through the compression fitting towards the frozen blockage and emits a stream of water under pressure from the pump that erodes and eliminates the frozen blockage, and return water is pushed from the blockage back to the return fitting and through the return hose to the container thereby providing a closed loop system"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water waste stream is pumped through a cavitation nozzle, desirable effects occur which result in ionization of the water which causes oxidation of the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water waste stream is pumped through a cavitation nozzle, desirable effects occur which result in ionization of the water which causes oxidation of the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "US-9604157-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the extraction mechanism 100 functions to remove contaminants, such as water and solid particulates from a pumped gaseous stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-9604157-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the upstream force can be applied by the water mass on the sealing member 400 (e.g., in conjunction with gravity, centrifugal force, or another exterior force), by pressure generated by the pump 40, by built-up pressure due to the contaminants blocking the flow of pumped fluid 13 through the selection mechanism 300, or due to any other suitable force"}, {"pat_id": "US-5326468-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water waste stream is pumped through a cavitation nozzle, desirable effects occur which result in ionization of the water which causes oxidation of the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "US-9611160-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "1d, a recirculation stream 38 returns part of the third treated stream 34, intermittently or continuously, to the anodic oxidation section 4 by tanks, valves and pumps (not shown) as required"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101173309-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to prevent the wear of the member due to the high speed flow, a filter (not shown) for trapping sand or the like between the inlet port 403 and the upstream side supply valve v1u on the downstream side of the pump p is appropriately used"}, {"pat_id": "US-8262752-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as another illustrative, non-exclusive example, frequent and sudden starting and stopping of the flow of feed stream 16 from the feedstock delivery system may affect components of the feedstock delivery system, such as by causing wear on a pump and/or drive system therefor"}]</data>
