  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-4570636-B2", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "in order to further reduce the momentum of the water flowing into the river water reservoir 2 through the dewatering pond 7, a concrete speed reducing block 8 is installed between the river water reservoir 2 and the diversion reservoir 7"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4570636-B2", "para_id": "para_13", "text": "as a result, the energy of the flowing water when colliding with the resin skeleton block 11 in the river water reservoir 2 is further reduced, and the water storage space formed by the resin skeleton block 11 of the river water reservoir 2 is less likely to be damaged"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, in order to prepare for the water shortage situation, there are ways to minimize the problems of securing the water by blocking the above-mentioned large artificial dam, reservoir or river water, and to secure the water that is insufficient without performing relatively large construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518747-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the shore protection block of the present invention can be installed in a lake, a dam reservoir slope, a river, or a ditch to provide a space where various aquatic plants, aquatic insects and fish can coexist along with water purification.10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102290035-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in the prior art, even if a fire-fighting helicopter wants to be supplied with fire-fighting water from a river, lake, or reservoir, the suction hose of the fire-fighting helicopter is blocked due to numerous floating objects in or on the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101048805-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as described above, the characteristics of the present invention is in the partition wall, the purpose of installing the partition wall is to induce the flow of water fines or contaminants contained in the river water this prevents sedimentation so that no blockage occurs at the bottom of the reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100748018-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, if the water stays in the reservoir for a long time, the contaminants are increased by condensation and contaminate the river water rather than being decomposed naturally"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100748018-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when this condition is continued and water is filled in the reservoir, contaminants, such as sludge, are deposited at the bottom of the river due to material lumping, as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101006852-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the partitions 12 and 13 induce the flow of the river water in the reservoir 11 so that fines or contaminants contained in the river water are not deposited so that the bottom of the reservoir 11 is not blocked"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101048805-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as described above, the characteristics of the present invention is in the partition wall, the purpose of installing the partition wall is to induce the flow of water fines or contaminants contained in the river water this prevents sedimentation so that no blockage occurs at the bottom of the reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "US-8074670-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this tendency is only amplified due to the fact that porosity reservoirs are typically constructed within the alluvial soils of a river bed so that there is an upstream and downstream portion to the reservoir corresponding to the overall valley gradient"}, {"pat_id": "US-8074670-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to a natural gradient of the land where porosity reservoir is formed (e.g., along a river bed), the reservoir defines an upstream end and a downstream end"}]</data>
