  <data key="d6">["locate", "expect", "leak", "be", "enter", "compare", "deduce", "include", "clean", "show", "base", "affect", "reach", "reduce", "take", "explain", "indicate", "associate", "analyze", "configure", "position", "inhibit", "increase", "understand", "preconcentrate", "treat", "filter", "perform", "determine", "detect", "obtain", "stimulate"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-11679993-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to the occurrence of biofouling, which is expected in a typical treated wastewater stream and associated wastewater handling equipment, it is beneficial for the tss sensor 5a to include a wiper system (not shown per se) which periodically cleans the face of the sensor component (not shown per se) of the tss sensor 5a"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101802534-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, in the effluent stream, the sensor may indicate whether the concentration of a contaminant, such as a biologically tolerant compound, a biologically inhibitory compound, and / or a compound that is generally resistant to biodegradation, has reached a predetermined value or trend, value, or trend, so that the controller can be stimulated to perform some action upstream, downstream from, or at the sensor from the sensor"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the contaminant were lead (pb) in this example, the conductivity of the water would increase from about 200 \u03bcs/cm in the feed water stream to 2000 \u03bcs/cm in the waste water stream, which would significantly increase detection sensitivity and reduce measurement time of the contaminant sensor 175"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the contaminant sensor 175 is positioned in the waste water stream, the detection sensitivity of the contaminant sensor 175 is effectively increased compared to positioning it the feed water stream"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the readings of the contaminant sensor 175 are affected by the water quality (which includes the water s chemistry and other factors) of the waste water stream, and the water quality should be understood to properly deduce the concentration of contaminants in the feed water stream based on the readings of the contaminant sensor 175"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "additionally, by positioning the contaminant detection system 170 in the waste water stream where ions of contaminants are preconcentrated by the water treatment module 110, the effective sensitivity of the contaminant sensor 175 is increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101802534-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, in the effluent stream, the sensor may indicate whether the concentration of a contaminant, such as a biologically tolerant compound, a biologically inhibitory compound, and / or a compound that is generally resistant to biodegradation, has reached a predetermined value or trend, value, or trend, so that the controller can be stimulated to perform some action upstream, downstream from, or at the sensor from the sensor"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the difference in the detected rates of temperature change during the wait period 695 is explained by the position of the first temperature sensor 414 being located downstream of the condensate management portion 400 (i.e., the drain pipe 394) such that the leaking water is inhibited from entering the drain line 398 to be detected by the first temperature sensor 414"}, {"pat_id": "US-11905688-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "9c, background noise is filtered from the sensor signal(s) to determine building movement, detect upstream leaks and possibly take remedial action in the depicted process 900-3"}, {"pat_id": "US-12264083-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the online multi-sensor module is especially configured to automatically analyze the water upstream of the treatment module, thereby obtaining one or more water parameters indicative of properties of organisms in the untreated water"}]</data>
</edge>
