ed by a product output sensor (e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in some embodiments, the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d may all be required to be less than the threshold in order for the controller 6034 to proceed to block 7840"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in some embodiments, if any of the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d are less than the threshold, the controller 6034 may proceed to block 7844"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "if, at block 7069, the system 6000 is currently in a normal water production mode, the target temperature 7068 along with a product or condensate output temperature 7070 determined from data provided by a product output sensor (e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in some embodiments, the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d may all be required to be less than the threshold in order for the controller 6034 to proceed to block 7840"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in some embodiments, if any of the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d are less than the threshold, the controller 6034 may proceed to block 7844"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "optionally wherein the drain blockage is determined by the controller (142) when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor (414) is about the same as the temperature reading of the second temperature sensor (418)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 142 is further configured to compare the temperature readings of the first, second, and third temperature sensors 114, 118, 122 to determine whether an error has occurred in the water heater 10 (e.g., leakage, drain blockage), as further discussed below"},