e contaminant sensor 175 is dependent on ph, temperature, conductivity, and ionic strength"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3032245-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "accordingly, whether the impedance response of interest is due to the liquid property of the circulating liquid and the electrode surface coating or due to the change in temperature is required to be known, which would otherwise provide a concern of malfunction of the anticorrosion performance degradation detection sensor 10"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3032245-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the impedance of the circulating liquid and the surface of the detection electrode 1 measured by the anticorrosion performance degradation detection sensor 10 increases by 2% when the temperature of the circulating liquid decreases by 1 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-10722824-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in second (sensor) compartment 23 to determine the temperature at the ph and corrosion sensors and permit correction of their readings"}, {"pat_id": "US-12163944-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "temperature sensors traditionally used within the industry are of resistive temperature detector (rtd) type, and are typically configured with a stainless steel dome to prevent malfunction due to corrosion and water ingress issues"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3706066-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "in another embodiment, not covered by the claimed invention, moreover the pressure sensor comprises another bragg grating, installed on a part of said sensor not deforming after pressure, such for example a cylindrical body, so that it is subject only to deformation due to temperature"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3706066-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "preferably, in addition the pressure sensor comprises another bragg grating, installed on a part of said sensor not deforming after liquid flow, so that it is subject only to deformation due to temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101967405-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore, if a point sensor is used to measure the temperature and strain in the water pipe, it is not possible to confirm the position of the sensor even if leakage or deformation occurs in the interval between the sensors"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3032245-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "accordingly, whether the impedance response of interest is due to the liquid property of the circulating liquid and the electrode surface coating or due to the change in temperature is required to be known, which would otherwise provide a concern of malfunction of the anticorrosion performance degradation detection sensor 10"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3032245-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the impedance of the circulating liquid and the surface of the detection electrode 1 measured by the anticorrosion performance degradation detection sensor 10 increases by 2% when the temperature of the circulating liquid decreases by 1 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, as noted above, the rate of deposit of lead oxide on the contaminant sensor 175 is dependent on ph, temperature, conductivity, and ionic strength"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101262046-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "various sensors such as temperature can be installed to detect the change of concentration of sterilization ion efficiently and actively.in order to efficiently generate concentration of sterilization ion through electrolysis when water passes, the electrode affects the flow rate of water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10753900-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "because the resistance of meas can directly demonstrate the electrode fouling status, the resistance of each mea sensors was used as an indicator of the whole mea and measured at ambient temperature (25 c.) using a digital multimeter weekly for 4 weeks to elucidate the electrode fouling influence"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "temperature sensor 38 is used to collect real-time temperature data and monitor the temperature of the incoming water to determine if conditions are conducive to pipe freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100385568-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this case, in the case of groundwater, after the operation of the temperature sensor 80 that detects the freezing temperature due to the characteristics of the groundwater, the water temperature (0) or more), it is preferable to have a timer to stop the continuous operation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100634761-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when it is determined that the communication state is good, the temperature data of the water tank together with the ambient temperature data (which can determine the possibility of freezing of the water pipe, measured by the temperature sensor) and (if the pump abnormality can be determined) preferably, a current sensor is further provided to control the pump using the current data supplied to the pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100643176-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is configured to prevent the phenomenon from occurring, and to prevent freezing and condensation due to the temperature difference between the temperature inside the sensor unit 52 and the sample when measuring the sample in a low temperature state"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to this aspect of the present invention, the water supply control device checks the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor and intermittently drives the pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe supplying water to the water tank of the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the outside air temperature falls below the reference value through the temperature sensor 270, the water supply control device 200 intermittently drives the pump 220 to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe 230"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the controller c opens the first opening / closing valve v\u2081 and simultaneously shuts off the second opening / closing valve v2 when the temperature sensor 13 detects the expected temperature of the freezing wave"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101207999-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "belt conveyor cleaning system having a pre-applied temperature sensor configured as described above is to clean the transfer belt by the cleaner system when the temperature is lower than the set temperature, and by washing water when the temperature is higher than the set temperature in winter if the wash water cannot be used due to freezing, the cleaning belt can be easily cleaned by the cleaner system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the temperature detection sensor 12 may be installed in a water pipe adjacent to the meter 11, that is, in an area of the water pipe where the freezing may occur most easily due to exposure to the outside air, thereby detecting the temperature of water in the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the controller 14 may be provided with information on the temperature of the water in the water pipe detected by the temperature detection sensor 12, and determine the freezing time of the water in the water pipe by grasping the temperature change of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the process of detecting the temperature of the water in the water pipe (s11), in the case of the general water pipe, the water pipe adjacent to the meter 11, that is, a temperature detection sensor installed in one area of the water pipe where the freezing can occur most easily due to exposure to the outside ( 12)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101365041-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "belt conveyor cleaning system having a pre-applied temperature sensor configured as described above is to clean the transfer belt by the cleaner system when the temperature is lower than the set temperature, and by washing water when the temperature is higher than the set temperature in winter if the wash water cannot be used due to freezing, the cleaning belt can be easily cleaned by the cleaner system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101404540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when there is a risk of freezing of the water meter m due to a drop in winter temperature and a rapid drop in the temperature of the tap water, the temperature of the heating wire w can be detected from the temperature information detected by the temperature sensor 100 and the flow rate information detected by the flow sensor 200, or not"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101508672-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the medicine dispensing apparatus according to the present invention is provided with a heat dissipating plate 70 inside the main body 10 to prevent the freezing due to heavy snow or cold in the winter and a temperature for sensing the temperature inside / a sensor 71 is further installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101541137-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "3, when the temperature of the ballast water w sensed by the sensor unit 300 becomes higher than the freezing point of the preset ballast water w, the control unit 500 outputs a drive stop signal can be applied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101942221-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the purging control unit 47 operates the freezing unit 43 and the heating unit 45 on the basis of the temperature information transmitted through the first sensor unit 33 and the second sensor unit 35 determine how many degrees the cooling or heating temperature should be adjusted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101961095-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by the temperature sensor and the power is supplied to the power storage unit 20, thereby preventing freezing of the main body 1 and the tube 70"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102193417-B1", "para_id": "claim_13", "text": "the method of claim 9, the driving step, the temperature measurement value derived from the temperature sensor is below the temperature threshold, when the humidity measurement value derived from the humidity sensor exceeds the humidity threshold to generate heat by driving the heating wire freezing prevention method, characterized in that"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102193417-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control unit determines whether or not a heating wire that is mounted inside the lower frame of the main body and prevents freezing of the side channel using the temperature measurement value and the humidity measurement value measured by the temperature sensor and the humidity sensor is driven"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102193417-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the step of determining whether the heating wire is driven by the control unit (s200), the control unit of the freezing prevention system determines whether the heating wire 300 is driven using a temperature measurement value, a humidity measurement value measured by a temperature sensor, a humidity sensor, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102193417-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, the temperature measurement value and the humidity measurement value transmitted through the data connection line 510 from the temperature sensor and the humidity sensor are compared with the temperature threshold value and the humidity threshold value, respectively, and the temperature measurement value is less than the temperature threshold value, and the humidity measurement value if it is determined that there is a risk of freezing or freezing above this humidity threshold, it is determined to drive the heating wire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102332096-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in this way, when the hot air blower is driven (by driving the heater 20 and the fan 30) to generate and blow hot air, the indoor temperature is measured through the temperature sensor 10, and the measured indoor temperature is above the freezing prevention safety temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102498793-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the heating element 40, the temperature sensor 64 installed in the water supply pipe detects the temperature of the water supply pipe, transmits the detected information to the controller box 60, and the controller box analyzes the detected information to determine the prediction of freezing and bursting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200310444-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention, by simply installing the device around the water pipe and connecting only the power supply, the sensor detects that the temperature drops to sub-zero temperatures and heats the heating sheet to prevent freezing phenomenon that the water pipe freezes or freezes in winter"}, {"pat_id": "US-10526548-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in one example, a low temperature fault may be determined and set in response to a low temperature signal from the temperature sensor 176, which may impact the ability to evacuate water due to freezing water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10898826-B2", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "if the air temperature sensor 140 is activated, the system 100 will stop operations due to an inability of the air heater with fan 143 to raise the wastewater temperature in the sump (bottom) of the container 139, 339 above the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "US-11047115-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it should be appreciated that if water temperatures are detected as being close to or below freezing, a pressure sensor may look for an increase in pipe pressure that may indicate freezing water in the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-11998860-B2", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "if the air temperature sensor 140 is activated, the system 100 will stop operations due to an inability of the air heater with fan 143 to raise the produced water or wastewater temperature in the sump (bottom) of the container 139, 339 above the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "US-12337259-B2", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "if the air temperature sensor 140 is activated, the system 100 will stop operations due to an inability of the air heater with fan 143 to raise the wastewater temperature in the sump (bottom) of the container 139, 339 above the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature rises above freezing, the sensor is de-actuated to interrupt the flow of electricity from the power source to the solenoid-actuated valve, and thereby close the valve and stop the flow of water therethrough"}, {"pat_id": "US-6436299-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the ambient temperature sensor circuit measures the ambient temperature of the atmosphere, so that the water treatment system can maintain a temperature level above freezing or some other predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-6436299-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the ambient temperature sensor circuit 114 measures the ambient temperature of the atmosphere so that the water treatment system 10 can maintain a temperature level above freezing or some other predetermined temperature setting"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 142 is further configured to compare the temperature readings of the first, second, and third temperature sensors 114, 118, 122 to determine whether an error has occurred in the water heater 10 (e.g., leakage, drain blockage), as further discussed below"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, should the controller determine that the tolerance has changed from 0.5 c to 1.5 c (one f to three f) between the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 114 and the third temperature sensor 122 during the standby mode, the controller may determine there is a leakage and indicate to a user to check the water heater"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in another example, when determining a leakage, the controller 142 may be configured to query the first and third temperature sensors 114, 122 during evening hours (i.e., sleeping) when it is most likely the user will not require use of hot water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "rather, only differences between the exhaust assembly 30 and the exhaust assembly 330 are specifically noted herein, such as differences in the positioning of the temperature sensors, and how the control system determines a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "10, the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 will increase (i.e., positive rate of change) again to a second peak or leakage temperature limit 690a after the water heater enters the standby mode from the heating mode"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in particular, the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 will increase to the leakage temperature limit 690a shortly after (e.g., about two minutes"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 detects a shift or change in state from the negative rate of change to the positive rate of change during the standby mode in which the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 begins to increase toward the leakage temperature limit 690a"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the difference in the detected rates of temperature change during the wait period 695 is explained by the position of the first temperature sensor 414 being located downstream of the condensate management portion 400 (i.e., the drain pipe 394) such that the leaking water is inhibited from entering the drain line 398 to be detected by the first temperature sensor 414"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "rather, the first temperature sensor 414 may be detecting a temperature of the residual condensate produced during the heating mode that has already begun to cool to a lower temperature (i.e., temperature lower than the leaking water) within the drain line 394"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the leaking water has reached a predetermined water level in the drain pipe 394, and the leaking water is then able to exit through the drain line 398 past the first temperature sensor 414"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "9-11, only the first temperature sensor 414 is used to determine a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "further, since any slight increase in the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 at the end of the wait period 695 might indicate that there is a leak, the controller may be able to detect even smaller leaks"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "9 represents another way that the temperature sensors may be positioned in a condensing water heater and used to determine a leakage in the water heater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100874616-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by filling the sensing unit, it is possible to prevent the malfunction of the leak detection sensor due to the small amount of condensate formed in the water supply pipe due to the difference between the water supply temperature and the room temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101406507-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, although the present invention is equipped with a pressure sensor for detecting a hydraulic pressure drop occurring when a water pipe leaks, and an acoustic sensor for detecting a sound wave generated when a water pipe leaks, a compact arrangement is possible, and a sound / pressure composite sensor which prevents excessive increase of the temperature of the leaked water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101803453-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6) in the same manner as the temperature sensor 110a, it is possible to detect that leakage occurs when the humidity value becomes higher than the second detection signal of the neighboring sensing unit 100 because the humidity becomes higher"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101803453-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if only the temperature sensor 110a is applied, if the temperature of the soil is lowered due to reasons other than leakage, in order to compensate for this, it is possible to compare the temperature and humidity sensing values together"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a single set of localized sensors (flow rate sensor 105, optional pressure sensor 65, optional acoustic sensor, and/or optional temperature sensor 93) can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 (126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "and a leak detector controller in communication with said first sensor and said second sensor configured to sense said ambient temperature from said first sensor and generating said drive signal to drive said second sensor to said elevated temperature greater than said ambient temperature and to generate a leak signal when said drive signal of said second sensor exceeds a leak point value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "claim_18", "text": "and a leak detector controller in communication with said first sensor and said second sensor configured to sense said ambient temperature from said first sensor and generating said drive signal to drive said second sensor to said elevated temperature greater than said ambient temperature and to generate said leak condition when said drive signal of said second sensor exceeds a leak point value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11905688-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "a water device with a pressure, temperature and/or flow sensor coupled to the fluid in a pipe or the plumbing system is affected by egress, flow, leaks, and use in the municipal water system"}, {"pat_id": "US-5638847-A", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "moreover, the moisture and temperature sensors may not be positioned to detect a leak, for incipient freeze condition, and thus, the flow sensor would provide the last line of defense to water damage"}, {"pat_id": "US-7549435-B2", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "in such a configuration, a sensor, such as a temperature sensor, may be included to determine the source of a particular leak among one of a plurality of fluid sources"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100874616-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by filling the sensing unit, it is possible to prevent the malfunction of the leak detection sensor due to the small amount of condensate formed in the water supply pipe due to the difference between the water supply temperature and the room temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a single set of localized sensors (flow rate sensor 105, optional pressure sensor 65, optional acoustic sensor, and/or optional temperature sensor 93) can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 (126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 142 is further configured to compare the temperature readings of the first, second, and third temperature sensors 114, 118, 122 to determine whether an error has occurred in the water heater 10 (e.g., leakage, drain blockage), as further discussed below"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, should the controller determine that the tolerance has changed from 0.5 c to 1.5 c (one f to three f) between the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 114 and the third temperature sensor 122 during the standby mode, the controller may determine there is a leakage and indicate to a user to check the water heater"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in another example, when determining a leakage, the controller 142 may be configured to query the first and third temperature sensors 114, 122 during evening hours (i.e., sleeping) when it is most likely the user will not require use of hot water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "rather, only differences between the exhaust assembly 30 and the exhaust assembly 330 are specifically noted herein, such as differences in the positioning of the temperature sensors, and how the control system determines a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "10, the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 will increase (i.e., positive rate of change) again to a second peak or leakage temperature limit 690a after the water heater enters the standby mode from the heating mode"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in particular, the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 will increase to the leakage temperature limit 690a shortly after (e.g., about two minutes"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 detects a shift or change in state from the negative rate of change to the positive rate of change during the standby mode in which the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 begins to increase toward the leakage temperature limit 690a"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "9-11, only the first temperature sensor 414 is used to determine a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "9 represents another way that the temperature sensors may be positioned in a condensing water heater and used to determine a leakage in the water heater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101803453-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6) in the same manner as the temperature sensor 110a, it is possible to detect that leakage occurs when the humidity value becomes higher than the second detection signal of the neighboring sensing unit 100 because the humidity becomes higher"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101803453-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if only the temperature sensor 110a is applied, if the temperature of the soil is lowered due to reasons other than leakage, in order to compensate for this, it is possible to compare the temperature and humidity sensing values together"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101967405-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore, if a point sensor is used to measure the temperature and strain in the water pipe, it is not possible to confirm the position of the sensor even if leakage or deformation occurs in the interval between the sensors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960008516-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, since the temperature sensor is weak to moisture, if the inside gets wet due to snow or rain when exposed to the outside, the temperature sensor often malfunctions, and there is a tendency for the risk of electric leakage and breakdown"}, {"pat_id": "KR-960008516-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, the present invention does not have any risk of moisture penetrating into the temperature sensing sensor effectively embedded in the cover even if it is hit by snow or rain as in the prior art, so there is no risk of leakage or risk of failure, especially the temperature sensing sensor is damp"}, {"pat_id": "US-10537921-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "reference symbol 21 designates a filter unit, reference symbol 23 designates a temperature sensor, reference symbol 25 designates a level sensor, reference symbol 30 designates an object loading unit, reference symbol 31 designates a door lifting drive unit, reference symbol 33 designates a washing lifting drive unit, reference symbol 11 designates spray nozzles, reference symbol 13 designates spray pipelines, reference symbol 15 designates a manual valve, and reference symbol 17 designates electronic valves"}, {"pat_id": "US-11659812-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the sensor 72c may also sense a temperature of the plurality of transmitting coils 721-724 and/or shielding layer 725 and provide a measurement to the power circuit device 715 so that a controller of the printed circuit device 715 may determine whether or not the wireless power transmitter 72 is overheated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102081866-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to avoid the use of expensive sensors necessary to withstand the temperature rise of the evaporator / condenser 4002, pressure sensors p e and p c correspond to the low temperature side of the heat exchanger 4004 and control valves v e and v c ) can be mounted on the fluid line"}]</data>
