imum water level, thereby causing the drain 1125b to be at least partially it will display that you are blocked"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102595234-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the evaporator tray 1125 further comprises an evaporator tray water level sensor 1171 arranged to detect when the water level in the evaporator tray 1125 is above a predefined maximum water level, thereby causing the drain 1125b to be at least partially it will display that you are blocked"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102807029-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control unit can block the inflow of water before the equipment inside the main body housing (10) is affected by the inflow of water through the water level sensor"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level of the pair of water level sensors installed in the snow channel changes, the blockage of the two water level sensors is determined by judging which of the three types of the fluctuations is the above-described pattern"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, since fluctuations in the water level are also observed in other water level monitoring panels in the system, the overall system determines the blockage position in units of sections where water level sensors are installed by comprehensively judging the detection results of each water level monitoring panel"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2780720-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, in consideration of the degree of water level difference between the two points, the absolute water level of each water level sensor, etc., the urgency of the water level rise due to blockage is divided into, for example, three stages, and only the alarm lamp is turned on in the first stage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841664-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101054375-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet port 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20 increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level in the pressure tank 314 is increased because the pressurized water does not flow smoothly into the flotation tank 200 due to the blockage of the microbubble injection unit 320, the water level sensor 334 detects the pump 312"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102490690-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "pipe blockage prediction system pipe blockage prediction system the present invention relates to a system for predicting pipe clogging, and more specifically, when a plurality of water level sensors are installed in a pipe through which sewage, sewage, rainwater, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101448435-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, due to the use of electrical signals by sensors installed in the water to measure the water level, breakage of electronic circuits due to lightning and short circuits frequently occurs in the summer, which is a problem, and repairing in the field is not easy, there are many problems"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "the method according to claim 1, wherein when the water level sensor senses water flowing into the sterilizing lamp due to breakage of the sterilizing lamp, the controller turns off the power of the sterilizing lamp, sterilization water purifier"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "wherein the water level sensor senses that water is introduced into the sterilizing lamp due to breakage of the sterilizing lamp inside the water reservoir, and the controller controls the power of the sterilizing lamp"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level sensor senses water flowing into the sterilization lamp due to breakage of the sterilization lamp, is configured to actuate the inlet valve to close the inlet tube"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the water level sensor 130 is configured to detect at least the water level sensor 130 in contact with the water flowing into the sterilizing lamp by the breakage of the sterilizing lamp at least before the discharge electrode"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101578433-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, when the water level sensor senses water flowing into the sterilizing lamp due to breakage of the sterilizing lamp, the controller 140 operates the inlet valve 150 to close the inlet tube, so as not to be supplied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101439225-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this case, as the water level l measured by the water level sensor 31 increases or decreases, the amount of the contaminants blocked by the screen member also increases or decreases proportionally to the internal water"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7709393-B2", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "in the present invention, the water level gauge 300 is preferably a non-contact type, and more preferably an ultrasonic type, from the viewpoint of the risk of false detection due to contamination of the sensor unit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100938251-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the first valve 500 and the second valve 600 are opened or closed at the same time, respectively, and received the displacement measured from the sludge detection unit 700 to determine whether there is deposition, and flows into the interior by the water level sensor 900"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101045390-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention as described above, the water level sensor detects the amount of manure contained in the manure tank to supply the electrolyte to the manure tank and the electrolysis device in accordance with the amount of manure contained in the manure tank to the manure of the appropriate concentration in the manure tank as it flows into the electrolysis device, there is an effect of uniformly treating the manure in the electrolysis device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another object of the present invention is to maintain a constant water level using a float valve and to supply a constant concentration of brine to the electrolysis tank so that sodium hypochlorite is equipped with an automatic valve and a flow sensor to produce a constant concentration of sodium hypochlorite it is to provide a generator"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0161641-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "another object of the present invention is a water level sensor failure detection method of the cold and hot water purifier that can prevent the occurrence of freezing of the cold water tank caused by the failure of the water level sensor of the cold and hot water purifier, a failure due to the overheat of the heater, or excessive waste of purified water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the leaking water has reached a predetermined water level in the drain pipe 394, and the leaking water is then able to exit through the drain line 398 past the first temperature sensor 414"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, the temporary storage tank of chemicals is formed by double walls of the outer wall and the inner wall so that even if the chemical exceeds the inner wall due to the malfunction of the water level control valve, it is protected by the outer wall as well as between the inner wall and the outer wall, that is, the leak detection sensor installed in the safety space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, the temporary storage tank of chemicals is formed by double walls of the outer wall and the inner wall, so that even if the chemical exceeds the inner wall due to the malfunction of the automatic water level control valve, it is protected by the outer wall, and between the inner wall and the outer wall, that is, a leak detection sensor installed in the safety space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, when a leak occurs in the water supply pipe 120, even if the water level of the water tank 130 continues to increase, the pressure sensor 140 may sense a low pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range, it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank, and also, if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor, such as leakage into the water pipe, the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101114764-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, there are advantages in that various accidents such as fire and water leakage, which may be caused by malfunction of the water level sensor, may be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is no local precipitation, but that there are water levels above a threshold, the control system 100 may track property operations to determine if there is a problematic operation that may be causing water leakage within the property"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, the temporary storage tank of chemicals is formed by double walls of the outer wall and the inner wall so that even if the chemical exceeds the inner wall due to the malfunction of the water level control valve, it is protected by the outer wall as well as between the inner wall and the outer wall, that is, the leak detection sensor installed in the safety space"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100932027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in particular, the temporary storage tank of chemicals is formed by double walls of the outer wall and the inner wall, so that even if the chemical exceeds the inner wall due to the malfunction of the automatic water level control valve, it is protected by the outer wall, and between the inner wall and the outer wall, that is, a leak detection sensor installed in the safety space"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0576981-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the sensor 51 also gives the possibility that when the water level in the washing chamber 21 drops, for example due to leakage losses, the vacuum blower 36 can be switched on again in order to compensate for these leakage losses and to always have a fully filled washing chamber available for washing processes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "as a result, the reliability of controlling the water level of the water tank can be improved, and there is an advantage that the control device does not malfunction by another even if an error occurs in any one of the pressure sensor and the angle sensor such as leakage into the water pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range, it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank, and also, if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor, such as leakage into the water pipe, the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101114764-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, there are advantages in that various accidents such as fire and water leakage, which may be caused by malfunction of the water level sensor, may be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399563-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the remote terminal device can determine and monitor the leakage of hazardous chemicals or the discharge of wastewater in the factory based on the gate status information and the water level information of the manhole water level sensor to be described la