  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101171869-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the pumping of the stream water 2 collected in the sump 120 continues while the collection efficiency of the screen 110 is lowered due to the blockage of the lower bed 4, the water level in the sump 120 is increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101054375-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and it is characterized by including a control unit to determine the state of the wastewater to control the water level of the sump, the ph and electrical conductivity and the flow rate of the reservoir, and connected to the level of the electrolytic cell and the positive and negative plates to control the electrolysis"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100531027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the rainfall and the level of rainwater and sewage in the sump tank 150 increases, the water level in the guide groove 141 is also increased to raise the lifting height of the buoyancy member 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100531031-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the rainfall and the level of rainwater and sewage in the sump tank 150 increases, the water level in the guide groove 141 is also increased to raise the lifting height of the buoyancy member 122"}, {"pat_id": "US-7802587-B1", "para_id": "para_25", "text": "thus, if float valve 10 were not in place, basement 61 could easily flood as the water level in sump pit 50 rises above sump pit lid 52"}, {"pat_id": "US-7802587-B1", "para_id": "para_29", "text": "float 11 lifts due to a rising water level in sump pit 50, thus causing float arm 14 to disengage rollers 16, 16 as it rotates"}]</data>
