nside the rainwater storage tank is rectangular or square hexahedron shape, side block, when assembling the stand block, the upper block and the lower block, it is difficult to correct construction errors and it is still difficult to solve the lower waterproof problem"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248434-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the purpose is to provide an inter-block coupling structure of a prefabricated rainwater storage tank that does not require filling work grooves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248434-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in this case, between the wall blocks 200 continuously arranged in the transverse direction to form the wall surface of the rainwater storage tank, the engaging portion of the recess portion 210 and the convex portion 220 is formed, and thus the strand wire 10 and the strand wire installation tool ( 100), the fastener 50, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, rainwater is circulated through the monthly circulation hole in the storage process, and a large amount of oxygen is supplied into the water, thereby improving water quality by natural purification.1 is a block diagram showing the overall prefabricated rainwater storage tank according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, the prior art of the above (1) to (4) is possible to change the shape of the storage tank to match the installation terrain by assembling the constituent block, but the problem that the manufacturing cost is high, the construction is difficult due to the large number of blocks there was"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102005372-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, even when the fixed mesh filter 110 is blocked, an appropriate amount of rainwater should be introduced into the float removing tank 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216793-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, it was configured to block rainwater flowing into the tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102430974-B1", "para_id": "para_22", "text": "in other words, when the torrential rain starts, an overflow phenomenon may occur due to insufficient space accommodated in the first storage tank 140, the second storage tank 220, and the permeable block 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102505041-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the filling pipe 52 is prevented from being clogged by foreign substances remaining in the rainwater flowing into the water collecting channel 41 of the road block 40, so that the filling pipe 52 flows into the water collecting tank 41"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, due to the overload problem of the above-described wastewater storage tank (30), it is inevitable to install the above-described frame (61) and rainwater blocking tent (60), which requires a lot of effort and cost"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, even if a rainwater blocking tent (60) and frame (61) are not installed in the car wash section (10) of the car wash, there is an effect of resolving the problem of overload caused by rainwater flowing into the wastewater storage tank (30)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore, to block the inflow of rainwater into the wastewater storage tank (30), the above-described rainwater inflow prevention device (100) is installed in the middle of the wastewater inlet pipe (40)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200148426-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to this, various flies and mosquitoes inhabited in the sewer pipe are blocked by the blocking plates 6 installed on the outer wall surfaces of the waste collection container 4 of the storm drainage tank 1 for roads, thereby preventing passage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, even with this method, it is difficult to completely remove the harmful contaminants that are strongly attached to the catchment surface by hydrophobic interaction, and the accumulated contaminants are gradually introduced into the storage tank over a long period of time during rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the continuous disinfection of rainwater in the storage tank requires expenditure of chemical costs, power costs, etc., and because the process is difficult to control and cumbersome, a more fundamental solution for removing the contaminants is required"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "thus, when rainwater is concentrated on the catchment surface 2 in which contamination by contaminants is prevented early by the titanium dioxide photocatalyst layer, the rainwater is transferred to the storage tank 1 through the catchment port 3 and stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the treated water through which the contaminant is removed by passing through the filter medium filling tank 71 is accommodated in the discharge box 91 by overflowing through the discharge unit 90, and then introduced into the drain pipe or artificial wetland through the drainage path 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, in the present invention, the removal of contaminants is actively performed on the road drainage during the initial rainfall stage in which the content of the pollutants is high, and the filter filling tank 71 considering the low amount of pollutants in the subsequent road drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is provided in the storage space of the treatment tank 6 includes a filtration device (9) for filtering and adsorption to remove contaminants contained in the road surface drainage rising from the lower portion of the treatment tank (6)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the amount of contaminants in the road surface drainage due to the subsequent rainfall is small, and it can be said that there is little problem even if the excess water is discharged immediately without passing through the filtration tank 54"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 30 is provided with a filter 31 for filtering contaminants such as organic substances, oil components, and suspended solids in the rainfall that do not settle in the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100784496-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the contaminants having their own weight among the contaminants included in the initial rainfall introduced into the first settling tank 10 are primarily precipitated at the bottom of the first settling tank 10 and do not settle in the first settling tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100786511-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "fine suspended matter having little specific gravity remaining after being precipitated in the contaminant treatment tank 13 is moved through the filter 20 installed in the upper part to the storm conduit 12 due to the continuous inflow of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the initial rainwater and sediment contaminants are completely excluded from the initial rainwater treatment facility 1 and the pressure or water level becomes zero, the drain pump 21 receiving the water is driven to operate the water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100927631-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, when rainwater flows into the sedimentation tank 200, heavy foreign matter such as sand sinks to the bottom and light foreign matter such as leaves or vinyl fragments rises on the surface of the water to easily remove contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100958442-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the conventional non-point contaminant purification device of the initial excellent excellent outflow water is the final outflow pipe line 21 only after the rainwater received in the median filling tank 13 and the settling tank 14 of the initial excellent purification tank 10 becomes the full water level"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100962546-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the contaminants accumulated on the bottom surface of the sediment holding tank 410 may be prevented from rising to the filter plate accommodating part 160 by riding the drain pipe 420"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100962546-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, particulate contaminants contained in rainwater fall into the sediment holding tank 410 and is confined"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, since the tip of the connecting pipe 50 is bent downward so as to be submerged in the rainwater in the sedimentation tank 10, contaminants having a small specific gravity such as oil floating on the water surface may not pass through the connecting pipe 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101181324-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, after treating the roadbed sediment and sediment contaminants contained in the sewage of rainy weather has been developed and used to flow into natural rivers or nearby sea, there is a storage tank type treatment device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202677-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this, the rainwater introduced into the water collection tank 40 along the raw water inlet pipe 46 may include a contaminant and mud not filtered by the screen filter 20 described above, the bottom of the collecting tank 40 there is an effect of sinking by spraying in the down direction of the sump (40)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101219791-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the method of claim 1, non-contaminant purification device characterized in that it further comprises a filtration tank connected to the rain pipe and the rainwater flowing through the flow passage of the rain pipe flows to remove foreign substances piggybacked in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101273679-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a contaminant separation tank 200 installed at a downstream side of the water collecting facility 100 to remove particulate contaminants from the rainwater collected by the water collecting facility 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101273679-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a contaminant separation tank 200 installed at a downstream side of the water collecting facility 100 to remove particulate contaminants from the rainwater collected by the water collecting facility 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101308064-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is settled down and the rainwater flowing into the purification treatment tank 21 through the drain hole 230 is supplied with a considerable amount of contaminants separated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, rainwater and contaminants from the side of the road 1 flow together through these steel gratings 102 and 104 and are then stored in the settling tank 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this way, in order to remove the sedimentary contaminants introduced with the rain water, the filter 120 is separated from the bottom 116 of the sedimentation tank 110 to perform the cleaning operation of the filter 120, and then coupled to the original position"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as shown, the primary penetrating paper 130 is positioned side by side with the settling tank 110, to remove and remove the floating contaminants primarily in the rainwater flowing over from the settling tank 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as shown, the primary penetrating basin 230 is located side by side with the settling tank 210, to remove and remove the floating contaminants primarily in the rainwater flowing over from the settling tank 210"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101358438-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 50 is supplied with rainwater from which sand and oil have been removed from the sedimentation tank 40, and various foreign matters contained in the rainwater [such as foreign matters of fine particles, etc., which are not sorted in the contaminant separator 20 and the sedimentation tank 40"}, {"p