940-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage and water treatment system using a multi-stage rainwater storage tank that can effectively remove contaminants contained in the rainwater in the process of collecting rainwater, and easy to clean the removed contaminants separately"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(2) since the filter which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is installed in the treatment tank, the drainage flowed into the inlet of the storm drain flows through the flow path including the maintenance tank and the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "road drainage with first flush treatment ability the present invention is to insert a filter filling tank having a filtration treatment function in the conventional rainwater receiver to the road surface drainage treatment device having an initial excellent treatment function that can reliably remove and treat contaminants contained in the road surface drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the treated water through which the contaminant is removed by passing through the filter medium filling tank 71 is accommodated in the discharge box 91 by overflowing through the discharge unit 90, and then introduced into the drain pipe or artificial wetland through the drainage path 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200358330-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a filtration member provided in the treatment tank and configured to filter and adsorb and remove contaminants contained in road surface drainage passing from an upper portion of the treatment tank to a lower side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200358330-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention actively removes contaminants from road surface drainage during the initial rainfall stage with high content of contaminants, and the contaminant content is less for road drainage than the treatment capacity in the subsequent treatment tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200431389-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 30 is provided with a filter 31 for filtering contaminants such as organic substances, oil components, and suspended solids in the rainfall that do not settle in the precipitation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200431389-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the contaminants having their own weight among the contaminants included in the initial rainfall introduced into the first settling tank 10 are primarily precipitated at the bottom of the first settling tank 10 and do not settle in the first settling tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "US-12202741-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, the particulates and other contaminants that can be dislodged and removed by backwashing the resin are caused to flow out the top of the tank, through the valve and are discharged to a suitable waste drain through the drain port c"}, {"pat_id": "US-8661819-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the contaminants may be removed from the heat exchanger in a generally non-invasive manner by periodically discharging water with the highly concentrated contaminants from a bottom drain of the heat exchanger (e.g., blow-down, blow-by, etc.) and directing the water to a containment location (e.g., evaporation pond or heat exchanger, storage tank etc.)"}, {"pat_id": "US-8776522-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the contaminants may be removed from the heat exchanger in a generally non-invasive manner by periodically discharging water with the highly concentrated contaminants from a bottom drain of the heat exchanger (e.g., blow-down, blow-by, etc.) and directing the water to a containment location (e.g., evaporation pond or heat exchanger, storage tank etc.)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3309310-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "rain overflow tank (1) according to at least one of the preceding claims, characterized in that a sensor device is provided and the degree of contamination of the retaining element (11) can be derived from the measurement data of the sensor device"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3466513-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "rain overflow tank (1) according to at least one of the preceding claims, characterized in that at least one sensor device (18a, 18b) is provided, and the degree of contamination of the retaining elements (8, 22) is derived from the measurement data of the sensor device (18a, 18b), preferably from the measurement data of two sensor devices (18a, 18b)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "thus, when rainwater is concentrated on the catchment surface 2 in which contamination by contaminants is prevented early by the titanium dioxide photocatalyst layer, the rainwater is transferred to the storage tank 1 through the catchment port 3 and stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the rainwater flows along the pipeline during the supply or discharge of rainwater, thereby minimizing contamination due to the propagation of microorganisms in the rainwater by maintaining uniform time of stagnation in the rainwater storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102281312-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to the instantaneous pressure and discharge, it is finely pulverized and stabilized while exerting a strong cleaning power, thereby preventing contamination of the inside of the storage tank 10 and the rainwater stored inside the storage tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102290677-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it has the effect of preventing clogging of the contact media and infiltration tanks, and contamination of soil and rivers.1 is a front view showing a rainwater treatment facility capable of excluding pipe-type initial rainwater according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "US-5736059-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the tank must therefore drain away into the lower heat exchanger and thence to the sewer when there is no wastewater flow, leaving the upper heat exchanger high and dry protecting the fresh water supply from contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102809593-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, it is a system that physically stores filtered rainwater in a rainwater storage tank without electronic devices by utilizing the gravity of falling rainwater, thereby reducing maintenance costs and providing a physical rainwater utilization system that does not require frequent maintenance due to corrosion or damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100955909-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in order to solve the problem that the contaminants accumulated in the inflow tank decay and cause odor after the rainfall is over, the hole is drilled at the bottom of the inflow tank, and gravel or porous media is installed outside to filter the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985170-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in order to solve the problem that the contaminants accumulated in the inflow tank decay and cause odor after the rainfall is over, the hole is drilled at the bottom of the inflow tank, and gravel or porous media is installed outside to filter the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101313936-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "naturally, the lower spigot 208 interlocked with the float opens, and after a certain period of time, the rainwater stored in the initial excellent tank is completely discharged to prevent decay due to the residue and to prepare for the next rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101316530-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, conventionally, when rainwater does not flow into the rainwater storage tank, there is a difficulty in treating the boiling point contaminants due to the decay of the stored water while the rainwater stays in the rainwater storage tank for a long time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101382006-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the conventional early rainwater treatment device has a problem that the residual water remaining in the treatment tank easily decays because (cause) the rainwater is filled up from the bottom to the height of the outlet even when the rainwater is stopped"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100800335-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "substantially, the rainwater treatment tank 22 is not likely to have the same internal diameter of the rainwater treatment tank 22 that is mass produced due to the high probability of shrinkage or deformation during drying (cooling), and the index plate 14 is coupled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100350735-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, during rainfall, the amount of sewage inflow is high and the flow rate is fast, so that the soil is not deposited in the sedimentation tank and flows into the dwelling house as it is, so that the cross section of the dwelling house 3 is reduced and the sewage terminal treatment plant is caused"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the removal process of pollutants deposited on the road surface is almost completed in the initial rainfall stage, and since the amount of pollutants in the road drainage due to the subsequent rainfall remains small, the road drainage does not come into contact with the media installed in the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101056650-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, the drain valve 158 is frequently opened to remove foreign substances when the rainwater reservoir tank 150 is cleaned or when foreign substances are deposited at the bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200171293-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, during rainfall, the amount of sewage inflow is high and the flow rate is fast, so that the soil is not deposited in the sedimentation tank and flows into the dwelling house as it is, so that the cross section of the dwelling house 3 is reduced and the sewage terminal treatment plant is caused"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the above structure can increase the treatment efficiency of high concentration pollutants drained through the road during the initial rainfall stage, but if it exceeds the treatment capacity of the maintenance tank due to the sudden rainfall, various pollutants deposited on the road are maintained"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, the removal process of the pollutants deposited on the road surface is almost completed in the initial rainfall stage, and since the amount of the pollutants in the road drainage due to the subsequent rainfall remains small, the road drainage is applied to the media installed in the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the removal process of pollutants deposited on the road surface is almost completed in the initial rainfall stage, and since the amount of pollutants in the road drainage due to the subsequent rainfall remains small, the road drainage does not come into contact with the media installed in the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100875260-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the case of such a buried water tank, the water tank is not affected by the external temperature as compared to the water tank installed on the ground and is not affected by the external environment such as rain or dust, and in particular, the water in the winter water tank is prevented from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, only the mechanical devices installed in rainwater pipes or storm water collection tanks do not completely prevent leakage of odors flowing back from the sewage pipes, and as a result, odor leaks around sewage pipes or storm water collection tanks, causing discomfort to passers-by"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "operation control for a time to remove the odor by the chemical reaction by ozone, but there is a risk that some of the odor may leak around the rainwater collection tank in the early stage of operation because the time required to reduce the odor by the chemical reaction of ozone and odor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101197024-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater penetration system of the present invention stores rainwater underground and partially penetrates underground to effectively inhibit rainwater leakage during heavy rains, and includes a sedimentation tank for depositing sand and foreign substances in water, and rainwater discharged from the sedimentation tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, only the mechanical devices installed in rainwater pipes or storm water collection tanks do not completely prevent leakage of odors flowing back from the sewage pipes, and as a result, odor leaks around sewage pipes or storm water collection tanks, causing discomfort to passers-by"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100531027-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the rainfall and the level of rainwater and sewage in the sump tank 150 increases, the water level in the guide groove 141 is also increased to raise the lifting height of the buoyancy member 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100531031-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the rainfall and the level of rainwater and sewage in the sump tank 150 increases, the water level in the guide groove 141 is also increased to raise the lifting height of the buoyancy member 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101154026-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after the manager removes the grating 23 to open the rain gutter 22 and connects the collecting rod to the lifting hook 27a on the ground, the container 27 is lifted to the outside of the rainwater storage tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "US-10865547-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a truly significant rain (storm) event, these storage tanks can be overwhelmed, thus resulting in flooding or discharge of excess storm water to the sewage treatment system, a body of water, or a river"}, {"pat_id": "US-11603651-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a truly significant rain (storm) event, these storage tanks can be overwhelmed, thus resulting in flooding or discharge of excess storm water to the sewage treatment system, a body of water, or a river"}, {"pat_id": "US-12209051-B2", "para_id": "para_84", "text": "when there is heavy rainfall, a reservoir or tank may become overwhelmed by a sudden rush of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101133580-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the sedimentation tank connected to the peripheral grooves is connected like the upper structure, and the drain pipe is connected to the peripheral grooves through the settlement, the solids constituting the impurities precipitated in the peripheral grooves are moved from the surrounding grooves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101367848-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after the completion of the red soil and topographical cleanup process before the start of the fresh water supply process further includes a drainage tank installation process for forming a drainage basin at a predetermined interval by digging a pit of at least 3 6m deep on the red soil it is also possible in form"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101367848-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the drainage tank installation process (s25) is a series of digging a pit of at least 3-6m depth at regular intervals in consideration of the soil depth on the red soil 20, inserting a predetermined drainage tank 22 into the pit, a series the process takes place"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101875497-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the sea water purification facility 120 can not process all of the contaminated water even though the internal water level of the shielding facility 110 is higher than a predetermined reference value due to a large difference between heavy rain, heavy rain or tide water, and transports the polluted water to the land-based storage tank 140 through the first pipeline 150"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100883436-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the case of storage tanks, heavy rains in summer require large-scale land or equipment, and if untreated water is kept, pests such as flies and mosquitoes are generated, which causes hygiene problems"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101219791-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the case of storage tanks, heavy rains in summer require large-scale land or equipment, and if untreated water is kept, pests such as flies and mosquitoes are generated, which causes hygiene problems"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681933-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the vertical void outflow facility to be installed in a tank or the like is provided with a strainer settled on a base made of steel or the like, attaching a sump bucket 90 at the lower part of the filter settled cylinder 31, and connecting the discharge pipe 91 to the sump bucket 90"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101366083-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if a problem such as a void occlusion occurs due to a pollution source generated during long-term operation, the filter can be easily washed and reused, and a predetermined size among rainwater flowing into the water collecting tank 10 through the water collecting inlet pipe 31"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101817003-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "next, the rainwater that has been purified through the water purification apparatus 2 is moved to the storage tank 3 along the connection line 52, thereby enabling a large amount of water to be supplied as moisture necessary for growing the water loss water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101345769-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the conventional wear and wash tank is provided with a movable beam that is opened and closed by a hydraulic cylinder for the fresh water and discharge of the rainwater or the initial excellent water, such a movable beam requires a high cost of construction, due to the nature of being submerged in water there is a problem that is not easy to maintain"}]</data>
