20 as the temperature inside the water tank (1) or less than 4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101693100-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in the above-described embodiment, although the water treatment system has determined to perform the chemical cleaning when the contamination index of the membrane filtration tank is equal to or greater than the second value, in another embodiment, the chemical washing is performed according to at least one of the temperature, as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102707115-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention provides an automatic chlorine injection device for preventing contamination of tap water in a public building water tank, which stores a large amount of chlorine in an automatic chlorine injection device and enables timely injection and replenishment, and also prevents deterioration of chlorine solution due to changes in ambient temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "that is, such a water tank is contaminated with water quality because the temperature of the stored water is increased due to the high external temperature of the summer, and the water quality is contaminated, and the contaminated water is not suitable for extinguishing, corrosion (mic"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "a temperature control device installed in the liquid corrosion tank to reduce an elevated liquid temperature of the liquid corrosion solution in the aerobic liquid corrosion tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the contrary, in the case where the mlss concentration is increased, the wastewater temperature in the tank is maintained at about 30 to 40 c during the biological treatment in the liquid corrosion tank, which is caused by the difference between the external temperature and the air supplied into the tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101151121-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this way, by crushing and homogenizing the organic sludge, it is possible to reduce the temperature, pressure, reaction time and the like in the subsequent reaction tank 5"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100315762-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the present invention, the composite panel 10 can be firmly assembled by fitting the composite panel 10 to the skeleton constituting each component panel of the large tank, so that the connection part of the composite panel 10 is caused by internal deformation pressure due to bending deformation or temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100988365-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the concrete tank exhibits deformation due to temperature deterioration, the cracks may occur in the panel adhesive composition of the concrete tank, resulting in a decrease in waterproofness and separation of the panel and the adhesive composition"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100271942-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "or higher, it is possible to prevent efficiency degradation such as nitrification reaction due to low outside air temperature during subsequent processing in the aeration tank 60"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101326272-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "as can be seen from the experimental results as described above, according to the embodiment of the present invention, it is possible to significantly reduce the amount of chlorate generated by appropriately controlling the supply amount of dilution water, supply temperature, flame generation concentration, and current density of the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "under the control of the drive means and the control means, the temperature of the cold water tank is raised to prevent freezing of the cold water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention has been made to solve the above problems, an object of the present invention is to determine the freezing of the cold water tank according to the changing product internal temperature and cold water temperature to determine the freezing of the cold water tank even in the winter at low room temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "four-way valve driving means for driving control of the four-way valve to prevent freezing of the cold water tank, it is characterized in that the compressor driving means for controlling the drive to increase the temperature of the cold water tank according to the control to prevent freezing of the cold water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is determined whether or not the preset ice generating temperature tcd (cold water temperature at which freezing occurs in the cold water tank)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result of the determination in step s18, when the internal temperature tr is not equal to or below the freezing internal temperature trs (no), the indoor temperature where the cold / hot water purifier is installed and the cold water temperature tc of the cold water tank 7 are the normal temperature condition illuminator returns to the step s15 and repeats the operation of the step s15 or less"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result of the discrimination in step s23, when the cold water temperature tc is equal to or higher than the cold water set temperature tcs (yes), it is determined that the freezing of the cold water tank 97 is completely removed, and the flow advances to step s24 to control means 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result of the determination in step s16, when the cold water temperature tc is equal to or lower than the freezing generation temperature tcd (yes), it is determined that the cold water tank 7 is frozen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to the temperature control apparatus and the method of the cold / hot water purifier according to the present invention as described above, it is determined whether the cold water tank is freezing according to the changing product internal temperature and the cold water temperature, so that the cold water tank freezes even in the winter when the room temperature is low"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100634761-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when it is determined that the communication state is good, the temperature data of the water tank together with the ambient temperature data (which can determine the possibility of freezing of the water pipe, measured by the temperature sensor) and (if the pump abnormality can be determined) preferably, a current sensor is further provided to control the pump using the current data supplied to the pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100875260-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the case of such a buried water tank, the water tank is not affected (affect) by the external temperature as compared to the water tank installed on the ground and is not affected by the external environment such as rain or dust, and in particular, the water in the winter water tank is prevented from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to this aspect of the present invention, the water supply control device checks the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor and intermittently drives the pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe supplying water to the water tank of the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194148-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the temperature is lowered, the outdoor temperature may not directly affect the water tank, thus delaying the freezing time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_11", "text": "or more, the water in the water tank 1 is heated and sterilized at low temperature, thereby suppressing the growth of microorganisms, in winter, when the temperature is 4 c or less, it is characterized in that the water in the water tank 1 is heated to prevent freezing due to the phenomenon of heat treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "thus, when the temperature of the storage tank 100 is below a certain temperature, the freezing prevention function operates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "maintaining the temperature of the purified water flowing into and stored in the purified water tank unit 1100 by the anti-freezing heater unit 1600 at any one temperature selected from the range of 27 to 75 degrees celsius is to promote the activation of the advanced oxidation process (aop)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200321853-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature falls below the freezing point, the built-in electronic temperature control device (2-15) of the pcb board (2-1) detects it and the hot water tank (2- by operating the heater 2-3 and the warm water circulation device 2-21 of 2), the temperature inside the system is increased due to electric heat dissipation, thereby preventing the freezing of the system at the source"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468890-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the user can adjust the temperature controller 32 so that the water (w) heating temperature in the steam tank 10 can be arbitrarily set to be heated, whereby the water (w) appropriately according to the freezing state of the freezing pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when freezing temperatures are sensed by the bulb, there is an outflow of water from the valve device and an inflow of water from the inlet conduit, thereby preventing freezing of water within the tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4936114-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "sufficient aqueous ice slurry is fed to mixing tank 22 by conduit 54 to keep the temperature of the liquid therein close to, but above, the freezing point so that there is no increase in ice particle formation"}, {"pat_id": "US-5816288-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "temperature variations, especially low temperatures below freezing, can cause the screens to frost over and become (break) damaged thus allowing an entrance to the storage tank for insects and other undesired elements"}, {"pat_id": "US-5876596-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after valve 44 has been open for a sufficiently long interval to permit the essentially deuterium free water from separator 28 to flow into tank 50, timer 62 or microprocessor 18 activates cooling element 56 to reduce (break) the temperature of the water sample to the freezing point (32 f.)"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in colder environments, existing exterior collection and storage tanks may crack or break when the temperature drops below freezing, and the water in the tank turns to ice"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature of the water in the storage tank falls below a specified temperature for a specified period of time, thereby indicating that the possibility of freezing exists, the microprocessor activates the pump to dump water from the storage tank through the alternate outlet to the alternate destination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101861072-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the thermal hydrolysis apparatus 65 is operated to remove the concentrated sludge from the sludge concentration tank 60 under conditions of high temperature (about 150 c) and high pressure (about 20 bar) to methane fermentation of the post-"}, {"pat_id": "US-6814866-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the typical net