-100499785-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100540762-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841664-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101054375-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet port 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20 increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level in the pressure tank 314 is increased because the pressurized water does not flow smoothly into the flotation tank 200 due to the blockage of the microbubble injection unit 320, the water level sensor 334 detects the pump 312"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365284-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101036584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the sludge storage tank 100 increases above a predetermined level, the flow rate controller 110 increases the output of the transfer pump 107 to increase the flow amount of sludge transferred to the cavitation storage tank 120, and the sludge storage tank 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101036584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the water level of the sludge storage tank 100 is 100 to 120% of the set water level, since the water level becomes the full water level, four cavitation generators 130 corresponding to four levels can be operated to greatly increase the throughput of the sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0137696-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "moreover, the method of checking the low water level in the water tank by using the air tank is very conventional, and it only functions to block the flow of water only when the water is almost full in the water tank, thereby making it difficult to identify the low water amount in the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "water purifier automatic drainage method of another embodiment of the present invention, the water level check step of detecting the water level of the water tank to determine the number of water, the step of determining the number of water to be confirmed for a certain time, and if a predetermined number or more is confirmed, drainage of the water tank and opening the valve and draining the water, determining whether the water level is confirmed within a predetermined time, checking the water level when the water level is confirmed, and draining the water by opening the water drain valve of the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100644949-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "third, when the water level is confirmed for a predetermined number of times or more, a drainage step of opening and draining the drain valve of the refrigerant tank, determining whether the water level is confirmed within a predetermined time, and a water level checking step of checking the water level when the water level is confirmed as a result, errors due to internal factors can be recognized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102391446-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "specifically, the control device 30 may determine whether filter cleaning is necessary by checking whether the water level in the water tank is equal to or greater than a preset threshold value based on the water level detection information"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "specifically, when the water level gauge 111 detects that the water level in the contaminant removal tank 110 is higher than the specified water level, control is performed to relatively increase the amount of water transferred by the advection pump 122, and the contamination level is also increased"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_28", "text": "for example, in the case of the water level gauge 111 having a configuration in which an on signal is output when the water level of the contaminant removal tank 110 exceeds a prescribed water level defined in advance and an off signal is outputted when the water level falls below the prescribed water level, the amount of effluent water can be derived from the time when the off signal switches"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100674176-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "since the second filtration system 40 is relatively small and runs for a long time, it filters out contaminants as much as possible, enters the filtered water into the water level control tank 10 and consequently returns it to the swimming pool"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the initial rainwater and sediment contaminants are completely excluded from the initial rainwater treatment facility 1 and the pressure or water level becomes zero, the drain pump 21 receiving the water is driven to operate the water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100958442-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "ho